{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths","id":495557,"title":"Open Development: Kiths","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-28T18:30:36-07:00","id":495557,"title":"Open Development: Kiths","content":"I dropped a bunch of Kiths. You should see. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths/\" target=\"_blank\"> Changeling the Lost Second Edition: Kiths &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T18:34:10-07:00","id":495580,"title":"","content":"I am seeing.<br /> <br /> I am being seen.<br /> <br /> I exist.<br /> <br /> Wait, wrong thread for that.<br /> <br /> *gets back to reading*<br /> <br /> EDIT: Heh heh, Kith Fads with Strangers. Like whenever a new supplement comes out, eh Jane?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T18:56:13-07:00","id":495600,"title":"","content":"Phew, those kith blessings have some bite to them, that's for sure. They're a lot more confronting than the odd extra dice or 9-again in 1E.<br /> <br /> I like the inclusion of greys! It certainly invokes that image really well. Also glad that you're using some of the ESP and psychic merits as flavour for some of them.<br /> <br /> The fact that Gravewrights can actually add anchors and other ghost-related conditions is awesome too, because it gives you the ability to actually ghost about when your abilities would be wasted a bit (as ghosts can be ridiculously variable in focus)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T19:00:08-07:00","id":495603,"title":"","content":"So, asking for clarity: Antiquarian Blessing refers to using Pscyhometry with Glamour rather than Willpower. Does that mean they can buy Psychometry as a merit, or they can effectively use it via their blessing?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T19:00:51-07:00","id":495604,"title":"","content":"I don't know if it's necessary, but specifying whether a Gentry can <i>change</i> a given changelings Kith after initially setting it would be interesting. Although, that may well open a can of worms with players wanting to change their Kith after escaping (which could probably be handled by making it a Gentry-only thing, or a result of the god-like power a Gentry has in their own realm, or something). Like, a Gentry grabs a person, initially decides he wants them to be a tree. Later on, he wants a monkey, but can't/can't be bothered going to grabbing another person or trading with another Gentry for some reason, so he grabs this tree and reshapes it into a monkey.<br /> <br /> Your phrasing implies that this is impossible, or at least very, very rare, but it was just a thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T19:04:05-07:00","id":495613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=495603#post495603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, asking for clarity: Antiquarian Blessing refers to using Pscyhometry with Glamour rather than Willpower. Does that mean they can buy Psychometry as a merit, or they can effectively use it via their blessing?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It'd be added in as part of their blessing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T19:06:16-07:00","id":495618,"title":"","content":"For the Leechfinger's Blessing, how does it interact with having the Hardy merit as is? Can a Leechfinger with Hardy \u2022\u2022\u2022 drain two health and have the equivalent of Hardy \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022? Could a particularly high Wyrd Leechfinger fob off like 10 glamour, draining some poor sods dry and be functionally immune to anything the merit covers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T19:08:29-07:00","id":495623,"title":"","content":"I feel like Draconic's armor has something bothersome to it, but quite can't put my finger on it. I'll come back to it later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T19:19:37-07:00","id":495632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=495623#post495623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like Draconic's armor has something bothersome to it, but quite can't put my finger on it. I'll come back to it later.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's the fact that it's a full coverage armour that scales with Wyrd. The thought of coming up against a high-wyrd draconic hunter/loyalist feels like the &quot;fond&quot; memories of fighting high toughness/resilience vampires in cWoD :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T19:22:22-07:00","id":495634,"title":"","content":"While I love that Firehearts can now essenitally always strike a match, I am deeply pleased with the maintenance of it as a mentally-based Kith while not keeping it exactly the same. That was always one of my favorite touches to the kith, and I got a lot of mileage out it. This is perhaps a saner take on it.<br /> <br /> EDIT:@Xen- It might be that, but 2nd Edition also does a lot more damage on the lethal and up spectrum, so it's not wildly overpowered.....maybe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-28-2015, 10:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T19:26:33-07:00","id":495636,"title":"","content":"Still going over the mechanics of these. I'll try to form a more coherent impression of the bits that seem problematic later.<br /> <br /> My positive impressions right now: Kiths make me want to make a character for this game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T19:27:54-07:00","id":495641,"title":"","content":"Okay, so changelings are all badasses and/or absurdly skilled in their peaceful area of expertise.<br /> <br /> I can dig it.<br /> <br /> Though...Chimeras are a bit too powerful. I like the idea they can adapt to magic thrown their way, but it makes more sense as a penalty to actually use anything against them rather than &quot;Oops, I have Glamor, your conjured raging inferno is a bit ticklish.&quot;<br /> <br /> Look on the Keeper's face should be <i>priceless, </i>though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T19:32:04-07:00","id":495646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=495636#post495636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My positive impressions right now: Kiths make me want to make a character for this game.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is literally the best thing we can hope to hear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T19:33:14-07:00","id":495647,"title":"","content":"Yeah, no, Changelings have clearly gotten tired of the under-powered commentary and decided to just collectively say &quot;Hey, remember when we were nature/dream gods?&quot;.<br /> <br /> I am not sure what to make of Ifrit's having pyrokinesis without the context of Contracts, but hell, I'll run with it for now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T19:35:15-07:00","id":495648,"title":"","content":"The nods to the metaphysics of Arcadia and the nature of the Gentry and general little details in the introduction write-up of the Kiths are fantastic. Just fantastic.<br /> <br /> And <i>all these flexible and flavorful Kiths</i>. And this is just roughly <i>a third</i> of what will be in the full book! I'm dumbstruck. In a good way. As most Onyx Path products recently have tended to leave me with the teases before release.<br /> <br /> Some of what I'm seeing in the mechanics probably bears discussing, but I'll be looking more carefully at them later. Right now, I need sleep. (And it's probably not going to come easy with all this swimming in my head!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 04-28-2015, 10:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T20:05:05-07:00","id":495664,"title":"","content":"So many squid references. {=:E<br /> <br /> My God, Razorhands are horrifying. Now I'm extremely curious as to what my favorite kith (Venombite) looks like.<br /> <br /> So, are the kiths with cultural names, like Ifrit and Nix, named such by the Gentry themselves because Keepers steal from human mythology?<br /> <br /> This is all super exciting. Thanks for sharing, David!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T20:35:02-07:00","id":495721,"title":"","content":"just started giving it a read can't wait to play Changeling again. you've made one of the best WoD games better. love the mix and match Kith/Seeming approach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T20:36:25-07:00","id":495739,"title":"","content":"I can't offer much of use regarding mechanics, what with not yet being well acquainted with GMC and being away from my books besides. However, this stuff makes me really, really want to<i> get</i> well acquainted. ^_^ I love these. I am really looking forward to the rest, and eager to see the illustrations I know some of these will be getting. Will all Kiths be getting visual aids?<br /> <br /> I admit I had wondered how effective the flash fiction was going to be, given the very tight space for description and mechanics, so thank you for shutting me up. I knew the Kith Blessings were becoming more robust and interesting, but -- despite my aforementioned inadequacies regarding mechanics -- it is very pleasing to see just how robust and interesting. Like others have said, every Kith feels like a badass or otherwise superbly accomplished at their respective areas of expertise.<br /> <br /> I also wish I had first finished the work I stayed late to finish, instead of taking a break to &quot;read just a little.&quot; XD Damn you all for doing too good a job for me to put it down! Gonna finish that work now, but more specific comments will probably come over the next few days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T21:13:20-07:00","id":495857,"title":"","content":"Making a note in case it isn't caught for the Nightsinger and Thusser blessings: there is no such Skill as Performance in nWoD \u2014 the Skill for playing music is Expression.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T21:42:18-07:00","id":495870,"title":"","content":"Maker's blessing seems to encompass and dwarf Smith's<br /> <br /> Illes could use a bump in power due to the heavy restriction of only working in the dark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":252,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","user":"basketcase","date":". 04-29-2015, 12:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T21:55:47-07:00","id":495878,"title":"","content":"Do razorhands do lethal or bashing with basic attacks? I know that spending glamour makes it aggravated though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T22:02:48-07:00","id":495894,"title":"","content":"Before I say anything else, I have to share a positive: I read the Antiquarian Kith and immediately said &quot;Dang. I'd actually want to play one of these now.&quot; Their powers were unique, useful, and distinguished them.<br /> <br /> My chief complaint is pretty much the antithesis of this. Some Kiths have powers that are basically &quot;+1 to Initiative and Defense&quot;, and that is just... Tremendously underwhelming. A small bonus to these will not provide the feeling of &quot;Wow, what a fae element&quot;.<br /> <br /> That aside, there's so much promise here, so... Thumbs up! Your team did great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T22:20:03-07:00","id":495919,"title":"","content":"I really like the limits on transformation now, wherein there's no 'too inhuman to escape the realm', instead you're only too inhuman while in Arcadia. Big thumbs up there.<br /> <br /> <br /> Kith blessings do seem to be a lot more potent now, which I like, though some are a little much (I'm especially not a fan of a kith allowing aggravated damage, considering 2nd edition has otherwise seemed to make aggravated damage harder). Regardless, the writing's good and I do love the diversity of the different mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 04-29-2015, 01:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T22:22:24-07:00","id":495925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingCarnival</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=495878#post495878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do razorhands do lethal or bashing with basic attacks? I know that spending glamour makes it aggravated though.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're considered weapons. So, lethal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T22:23:14-07:00","id":495926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=495857#post495857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making a note in case it isn't caught for the Nightsinger and Thusser blessings: there is no such Skill as Performance in nWoD \u2014 the Skill for playing music is Expression.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. Done and done. <br /> <br /> This sort of thing happens with first drafts. However, I'm going to make a point of being thorough. I know Changeling 1e has a few of these problems that made it into print. I'd rather they not get that far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T22:23:54-07:00","id":495927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=495894#post495894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before I say anything else, I have to share a positive: I read the Antiquarian Kith and immediately said &quot;Dang. I'd actually want to play one of these now.&quot; Their powers were unique, useful, and distinguished them.<br /> <br /> My chief complaint is pretty much the antithesis of this. Some Kiths have powers that are basically &quot;+1 to Initiative and Defense&quot;, and that is just... Tremendously underwhelming. A small bonus to these will not provide the feeling of &quot;Wow, what a fae element&quot;.<br /> <br /> That aside, there's so much promise here, so... Thumbs up! Your team did great.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome. I'll be mindful of those things, and see if I can't kick them up a notch in redlines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T22:30:32-07:00","id":495931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=495634#post495634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I love that Firehearts can now essenitally always strike a match, I am deeply pleased with the maintenance of it as a mentally-based Kith while not keeping it exactly the same. That was always one of my favorite touches to the kith, and I got a lot of mileage out it. This is perhaps a saner take on it.<br /> <br /> EDIT:@Xen- It might be that, but 2nd Edition also does a lot more damage on the lethal and up spectrum, so it's not wildly overpowered.....maybe.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I like how the Ifrits can psychokinetically manipulate any fire around their vicinity without a contract. They set a building on fire, and everybody inside becomes their bitch!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T00:50:03-07:00","id":496033,"title":"","content":"So I have a question about kith blessings- some of these effectively give merits, although so far all I've noticed are supernatural merits, do these blessings count as having the prerequisites for being able to buy stuff?<br /> <br /> Say the writer of hurt locker makes that martial art based on psychokinesis not a supernatural merit, could an ifrit buy it? Or would they have to buy a contract to further manipulate fire like any other changeling?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T00:50:40-07:00","id":496035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=496033#post496033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So I have a question about kith blessings- some of these effectively give merits, although so far all I've noticed are supernatural merits, do these blessings count as having the prerequisites for being able to buy stuff?<br /> <br /> Say the writer of hurt locker makes that martial art based on psychokinesis not a supernatural merit, could an ifrit buy it? Or would they have to buy a contract to further manipulate fire like any other changeling?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it gives a Merit, you get it. You don't need the prerequisites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T01:27:13-07:00","id":496053,"title":"","content":"Well good to know, but my question was in fact the direct opposite of the one you answered (lol) - Do merits gained through seemings, temporarily or permanently, count as prerequisites enabling the changeling to buy other merits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T02:14:06-07:00","id":496102,"title":"","content":"Love these. As others have said, they make me excited to play the game. I particularly enjoy the Kiths based on specific folklore (Thusser, Brollachan, etc.) interspersed with the more general types of Fae creatures.<br /> <br /> Though I think the Greys fall outside that thematic frame. While I would agree cryptids and urban legends are modern folklore, working in aliens strikes me as too wild a departure from the timeless magical creatures Changeling otherwise draws from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://twitter.com/carykingdom\" target=\"_blank\">@CaryKingdom </a>- Writer and Ne'er-do-well<br /> Deititian at <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/category/worlds/scion/\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Second Edition</a><br /> Storyguide of <a href=\"https://scabbyrooster.fandom.com/wiki/The_Demi_Dozen\" target=\"_blank\">The Demi Dozen</a>, a Hero-level, live-streamed Scion Campaign<br /> Everything is subject to change; all opinions expressed are solely my own or those of my houseplants.","edited":{"userid":1093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1093-arlecchino","user":"Arlecchino","date":". 04-29-2015, 05:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1093-arlecchino","name":"Arlecchino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T02:43:53-07:00","id":496109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=496053#post496053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well good to know, but my question was in fact the direct opposite of the one you answered (lol) - Do merits gained through seemings, temporarily or permanently, count as prerequisites enabling the changeling to buy other merits?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh! Yes. They'd count. So our Ifrit could pick up some of the Psychokinesis Merits from Hurt Locker, theoretically. I'll make that clearer. This would bypass some of the normal limitations on Supernatural Merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T03:24:47-07:00","id":496143,"title":"","content":"I don't know about the Aggravated damage from the Razorhands... I mean, 2e has generally been very shy about giving out powers that do Aggravated damage, and here we have a kith which can do it, basically, for free? Wouldn't 8 Again on Brawl attacks fit better with the rest of the edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T03:51:43-07:00","id":496171,"title":"","content":"As my group's Onyx Path fanboy and basically one-way liaison, I've thus-far immediately recited anything Changeling related to everyone when I see them. This update continues the trend, except first I read it to myself twice and have more-or-less been nonstop thinking of characters to play. This stuff is fantastic and I love it -- even moreso because I know quality like this will tilt my friends that have been on the fence about Changeling.<br /> <br /> Draconic seems a little strong, but it's effective opposite (the Razorhands) puts the offense/defense balance more or less where I'd want it to be. Though, maybe 1+(Wyrd/2) for the Razorhands' damage? <br /> <br /> I'm a little wary with how specific the Kith physical descriptions are, unless most are just examples? I like the idea of looking at a Changeling and not *necessarily* knowing their Kith, simply out of love for information games. So I guess this is less feedback and more inquiring if two, say, Brollachan Beasts were next two each other would any Lost onlooker know immediately that they are of the same Kith? Or is there sufficient room for deviation?<br /> <br /> In any case, to reiterate: absolutely fantastic work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T05:18:25-07:00","id":496191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arlecchino</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=496102#post496102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I think the Greys fall outside that thematic frame. While I would agree cryptids and urban legends are modern folklore, working in aliens strikes me as too wild a departure from the timeless magical creatures Changeling otherwise draws from.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that is intentional. In the write-up it is mentioned the Kiths change with human culture and the evolution of myth and stories, as in the end the Gentry only have as much imagination as the human collective they draw from for inspiration. So it says something very interesting that one of the Kiths existing in the current day is in fact inspired by the idea of Grey aliens. They are a legend of the modern era, as much as dragons, barghest, wendigos, sidhe and what have you come from folklore that has existed for a long time and proliferated through the human mind.<br /> <br /> Besides, this is hardly the first mention of the True Fae taking inspiration from alien abduction stories and alleged extraterrestial contacts influencing some of the Others in how they present themselves or treat their captives. Alien abduction is the &quot;spirited away&quot; of 20th and 21st century pop culture. In my opinion, it makes perfect sense for the Greys to be present in this capacity in the 2nd edition. It gives the kiths and the Gentry a real sense of dynamic substance accompanying the progress of real world ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 04-29-2015, 08:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T06:41:25-07:00","id":496222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=496109#post496109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh! Yes. They'd count. So our Ifrit could pick up some of the Psychokinesis Merits from Hurt Locker, theoretically. I'll make that clearer. This would bypass some of the normal limitations on Supernatural Merits.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is going to be FUN!<br /> <br /> Anyway, these guys are downright awesome! Can't wait to see more!<br /> <br /> Though, while the Metalflesh are particularly cool, I have to ask something. When their write-up says &quot;their fists and feet do lethal damage&quot; and &quot;gain armor piercing 1 on all strikes made with their hands and feet&quot;, do you mean their unarmed attacks are lethal and can gain armor piercing 1 for a point of Glamour, or specifically attacks made with their hands and feet. If the second, would it be considered rude if I were to ask why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T06:54:49-07:00","id":496228,"title":"","content":"With the Leechfinger blessing, does it provide healing <i>in addition to</i> the downgrading agg/gaining dots in Hardy, or does downgrading agg/gaining Hardy supplant the 'standard' use of the power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T07:02:43-07:00","id":496232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arlecchino</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=496102#post496102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Love these. As others have said, they make me excited to play the game. I particularly enjoy the Kiths based on specific folklore (Thusser, Brollachan, etc.) interspersed with the more general types of Fae creatures.<br /> <br /> Though I think the Greys fall outside that thematic frame. While I would agree cryptids and urban legends are modern folklore, working in aliens strikes me as too wild a departure from the timeless magical creatures Changeling otherwise draws from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering aliens are the direct spiritual successor to the fae, I disagree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T07:06:31-07:00","id":496240,"title":"","content":"Damn! For every second edition game that starts open development, I want to relaunch my old 1st Ed games. Especially Mage, Werewolf and Changeling, these are my babies. So, excellent job, Onyx Path!<br /> <br /> One little criticism, though: I've read one too many Elemental description that starts like &quot;A statue made of...&quot; for my liking. I know many formerly-Elemental kiths are now in 2nd ed and it may be challenging to provide with more variety, but perhaps this could be addressed in the development?<br /> <br /> You are making a wonderful game into an even better game! That's something. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T07:41:44-07:00","id":496260,"title":"","content":"Are Kiths going to be able to be changed after one escapes? I've found stories like that quite enjoyable. Also, are we going to see Dual Kiths, with the powering up of Kiths?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/287-wildfire","name":"Wildfire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T07:47:22-07:00","id":496275,"title":"","content":"Too bad my group broke up, this convinced me to actually consider playing, instead of just hanging around and watching.<br /> <br /> Now I'm going to have to save up for even more books (My current queue seems to be EX3 &gt; GMC &gt; W:TF2 &gt; C:TL2?), also, find a new group...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T07:55:18-07:00","id":496285,"title":"","content":"Oh, another question of semantics for rules - when a Levinquick with a natural speed of 10 spends 2 glamour, does their speed become 60 ([10x3]x2) or 90 ([10x3]x3). I could se an argument for either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T08:44:07-07:00","id":496333,"title":"","content":"Wow, I mean wow. Changelings have received some serious upgrade haven't they?<br /> Now seriously changeling the lost is my favorite line from the new world of darkness but both me and my players had always one complain: they felt too weak and limited compared with the other supernaturals but now? You have made me fall in love whit this game all over again, all the kiths feel like such badasses. Hell I can't wait to see the contracts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 04-29-2015, 12:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T09:35:31-07:00","id":496375,"title":"","content":"I like this new approach to building powers that started in Werewolf and continues here, what with using existing mechanics rather than having to build native mechanics for each splat to do the same things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T09:59:09-07:00","id":496394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=496375#post496375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this new approach to building powers that started in Werewolf and continues here, what with using existing mechanics rather than having to build native mechanics for each splat to do the same things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aye, big time. Seeing it in action helps me feel glad Exalted's devs are taking a similar approach. Creating sufficiently robust systems and options as hooks on which to hang a wide array of different effects is a great way to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Minor tweakery. 04-29-2015, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T10:20:27-07:00","id":496413,"title":"","content":"Well alright, kith stuff is up!<br /> <br /> <b>Yay: </b>Kith blessings are pretty strong, wow. I like the addition of Greys. Not a whole lot was shaken up here, but it does give us a solid idea of how Kiths are going to intersect with Seemings (Side Note: They're way less subtle than I was expecting, daaang). Also I liked the descriptions/breakdowns of Kiths for the most part.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Nay: </b>Agreeing that Razorhands' being able to drill people with Agg is a bit much, I think 8-Again would probably be a bit more reasonable without sacrificing the concept.<br /> <br /> Also I feel like some of the fluff blurbs could stand to get another once-over, I don't really feel like they're communicating what the Kith is about so much as describing someone from the Kith just sort of hanging out. Relating to that, this might just be me, but anytime someone makes like a overly dramatic threat to hurt/kill a person (especially over minor annoyances or inconveniences) it just feels kind of petty. Like if its presented as an issue with handling emotions or being immature or w/e then yeah that's cool, but when its like &quot;Don't like my music, do you?&quot; it comes across as bit too juvenile for me. <i>Edit: Also yeah, I know they're only like a couple sentences, so it's a relatively minor complaint, all things considered.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>???: </b>So are Wizened now about using your skills/crafts to self-augment? Because that's the vibe I'm getting from their blurbs. Could be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3738,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","user":"Illuminated Minutia","date":". 04-29-2015, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T10:22:05-07:00","id":496415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=496143#post496143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know about the Aggravated damage from the Razorhands... I mean, 2e has generally been very shy about giving out powers that do Aggravated damage, and here we have a kith which can do it, basically, for free? Wouldn't 8 Again on Brawl attacks fit better with the rest of the edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>So far every supernatural has <i>some</i> method of doing it. Vampires have Claws of the Unholy. Mages have unravelling spells. Werewolves have teeth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T10:51:20-07:00","id":496431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=496415#post496415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far every supernatural has <i>some</i> method of doing it. Vampires have Claws of the Unholy. Mages have unravelling spells. Werewolves have teeth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but so far we've got:<br /> - A 1 dot Merit with a 4 dot Discipline prerequisite that you have to be in Frenzy to use and costs 1 Vitae.<br /> - A 4 dot Practice that costs an extra point of Mana and extra die of Reach to upgrade from lethal to aggravated.<br /> - A willful act of cannibalism and violation of the oath of the moon that only works on humans, wolves, and werewolves.<br /> - A free benefit from your X-splat that costs a point of Glamour to upgrade to aggravated.<br /> <br /> One of these things is not like the others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-29-2015, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T10:56:30-07:00","id":496434,"title":"","content":"CotU is only one dot, but I guess I see your point. <br /> <br /> On the other hand, it's something only 1% of changelings can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T12:09:21-07:00","id":496574,"title":"","content":"Jeez this makes me wanna play <b>Changeling </b>again. Day-umn.<br /> <br /> Does a Mirrorskin just mundanely disguise herself, albeit supernaturally fast/well, or is there a bit of minor shapeshifting involved to back it up? That felt like the implication, but it's a little unclear, at least from a narrative perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T12:36:57-07:00","id":496605,"title":"","content":"I noticed Lurkers got their 9/8 again taken away, but Inventors (Makers) kept theirs. Is this deliberate, or due to the Darkling Seeming abilities?<br /> <br /> I also noticed Tunnelgrub is gone. Is it intended to stay gone or be added later?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T12:40:41-07:00","id":496611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=496434#post496434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">CotU is only one dot, but I guess I see your point.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, it's something only 1% of changelings can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes it worse, not better, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T12:57:26-07:00","id":496639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=496605#post496605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also noticed Tunnelgrub is gone. Is it intended to stay gone or be added later?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't worry. The Kith list is only about a third of the ~100 planned Kiths for the core book. Dave's expressed an intent to hit pretty much every 1e Kith that doesn't get folded out for redundancy. I'm presuming Tunnelgrub's still going to be a thing, just like some others I noticed that weren't present, such as Broadback, Cleareyes, Minstrel, Windwings, and Flowerings. The last of those was even alluded to in the introductory text on Kiths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T12:59:12-07:00","id":496642,"title":"","content":"Love the Kiths.<br /> <br /> Gravewrights blessing needs to be clearer that when you add a condition to a place, object, or person, that you are doing so on behalf of a ghost/spirit/whatever and not yourself, because I don't know what a Gravewright would do with an anchor for example.<br /> <br /> Also its not clear if the ghost has to be present to say set up a new anchor for it, although I assume only an anchor has to be present to remove the anchor condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 04-29-2015, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T12:59:27-07:00","id":496643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=496605#post496605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also noticed Tunnelgrub is gone. Is it intended to stay gone or be added later?</div> </div> </div> </div>They said this is only a third of the total kiths, with that amount of variety, I imagine the only ones they really didn't keep were ones that were essentially the same kind of kith in a different seeming. (Like Firehearts and Flamesirens, Stonebones and Earthbones, Woodblood and Flowering or Swimmerskin, Waterdwellers, and Waterborn.)<br /> <br /> The most I can think in terms of tunnelgrubs is that they and skitterskulks might be folded into the same kith, since both have the same concept of &quot;creepy-crawly sneaking in tight dark places.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5823-ravian3","name":"Ravian3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T13:14:35-07:00","id":496672,"title":"","content":"Reading half the spoiled document I must say I really like a concepts, like inhuman Mien in Arcadia, Or evolution from Kith to Seeming. Also, including the Greys as modern abudction myth represantation.<br /> <br /> But I do not like the progress of character features the Kith adds - like Levinquick are about being electicity. In your Durance you are <b>living lghting</b> in Arcadia. So Elementals of them are &quot;clouds&quot; of electicty on the end. But if your Levinquick becomes Ogre, he gets to look like &quot;troll with sparks&quot;? And Darklings are hairless monstroiseties with arcs istead of hands?<br /> <br /> So from character perspective in one moment you are living electircty, then definy your Keeper, and SHAZAM, you have now troll-like body? Or hairless ape?<br /> <br /> Something like you are all Durance this...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://noarizona.files.wordpress.com/2013/06/electricitymonster.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> and in second change in to this?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://th00.deviantart.net/fs71/200H/i/2013/178/f/e/ogre_mage_lightning_by_frost0016-d6avlwb.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> This seems very odd...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=496413#post496413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>???: </b>So are Wizened now about using your skills/crafts to self-augment? Because that's the vibe I'm getting from their blurbs. Could be interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also get vibe that they are like Franskenstein-like parts exchanger. But what about all the fairy tales dwarves, gnomes, pixies and all this &quot;little people hard working thier magic&quot; that Wizined were in 1ed? Basiclly, who will now have mine True Fae Santa Clause in this slaverish toy factory as &quot;worker elves&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-29-2015, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T13:22:26-07:00","id":496691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=496672#post496672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So from character perspective in one moment you are living electircty, then definy your Keeper, and SHAZAM, you have now troll-like body? Or hairless ape?</div> </div> </div> </div>Who said it was instant? Pretty much every piece of fiction about the escape has the changeling struggling to escape, running through the Hedge, and having pieces of their soul torn away in the process (or something similar to that).<br /> <br /> For your lightning cloud, it could go like this:<br /> <br /> The cloud begins to remember that its a person, the loose cloud form starts to shape itself into a humanoid form, then as they make their escape the Hedge thorns tear pieces of the cloud stuff off leaving something that looks closer to the original human but with aspects of both the Kith and Seeming reflected in the new Mein of the Changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T13:30:16-07:00","id":496700,"title":"","content":"I am having a lot of trouble getting Google Docs to play nice right now, can this get mirrored somewhere else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T13:31:55-07:00","id":496705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=496605#post496605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I noticed Lurkers got their 9/8 again taken away, but Inventors (Makers) kept theirs. Is this deliberate, or due to the Darkling Seeming abilities?</div> </div> </div> </div> They aren't necessarily Darklings, so I wouldn't assume so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T13:36:49-07:00","id":496708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=496672#post496672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading half the spoiled document I must say I really like a concepts, like inhuman Mien in Arcadia, Or evolution from Kith to Seeming. Also, including the Greys as modern abudction myth represantation.<br /> <br /> But I do not like the progress of character features the Kith adds - like Levinquick are about being electicity. In your Durance you are <b>living lghting</b> in Arcadia. So Elementals of them are &quot;clouds&quot; of electicty on the end. But if your Levinquick becomes Ogre, he gets to look like &quot;troll with sparks&quot;? And Darklings are hairless monstroiseties with arcs istead of hands?<br /> <br /> So from character perspective in one moment you are living electircty, then definy your Keeper, and SHAZAM, you have now troll-like body? Or hairless ape?</div> </div> </div> </div>To reiterate a common note from the document, all of the depictions and descriptions are examples, not the only possible standards. A Levinquick in Arcadia could have been human-shaped, a &quot;cloud&quot; of electricity, or whatever else it pleases one to imagine. You also seem to have missed that this is independent of Seeming, and is simply the nature of how the Gentry's reshaping magics work:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Limits of Transformation</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Within their Keeper's realm, a changeling who appears as a human-shaped fire in the mortal world could have been a stationary pillar of flame, a wandering bonfire or even a single tongue of flame that was part of a vast fiery plain. The form that any changeling had in Arcadia may have been far less human than the form the changeling takes when they return to the mortal world.<br /> ...<br /> One fireheart may have spent her entire time in Arcadia as a swift messenger whose form closely resembles her Mask, while another might have been a roaring fire in a his Keeper's great hall, or the night light her Keeper chatted with before sleeping.</div> </div> </div> </div>The main reason it feels weird to you is because you seem to be playing down or ignoring that the Changeling taking back his agency is A Big Deal. Under the Wyrd's auspices and in the place of metaphor and allegory that is Arcadia, it's significant enough to bring on a second transformation resonant with the claimed Seeming, albeit still within the Kith's milieu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T14:27:24-07:00","id":496784,"title":"","content":"Think of an Ogre levinquick being more thunder than lightning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T15:04:47-07:00","id":496807,"title":"","content":"There is 32 kiths revealed. That leaves at least 68 kiths left.<br /> <br /> I'm going to make a guess as to how Romancer works.<br /> <br /> You get 2 dot striking looks merit , and by spending a Glamour point you can give someone your seducing the Swooning or Wanton conditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T15:16:56-07:00","id":496814,"title":"","content":"Speaking of the Gravewight blessing, another note: Reaching isn't a thing for non-spirit ephemeral beings, seeing as it's specifically a way to operate through the Gauntlet, and thus should probably not be on the list of Conditions the changeling can add or subtract. Relatedly, Materialized applies to the ghost, and thus should probably not be on the list of Conditions if the Gravewight's target is the thing supporting the ghost's manifestation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 04-29-2015, 06:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T15:49:39-07:00","id":496839,"title":"","content":"I have an idea for an Darkling Iles called Sister Mary/Ecstasy, a nun of Icelandic desent, who was as unattractive as she was faithful to Jesus. A Keeper was attracted to her suppressed desires, and kidnapped her to Arcadia. Becoming an Iles split her personality in two, in daylight she is Sister Mary, chaste, worshipful, compassionate, and humble, a paragon of temperence. By night she is Ecstacy, stripper, escort, pornstar, party girl. They have an uneasy truce, Sister Mary sees Ecstacy as her sins being purged, seperated from her, making her purer, and Ecstacy couldn't care a less about Sister Mary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T15:50:42-07:00","id":496840,"title":"","content":"In general I really like the direction most of the 2e stuff has taken, but I have one major concern to voice. Armor has a serious potential to imbalance combat in a way that impacts fun for the whole motley and I'm seeing kiths with the potential to stack a lot of it. It's really, really easy to wind up with a tanky character who can't even be significantly harmed by anything that wouldn't kill other members of the motley in two hits, which in turn leads to long slug fights while the rest of the motley hides or rolls to dodge every turn. I had a Summer Court Fireheart/Metalflesh and this became a serious issue with just two points of magical armor in excess of my Motley. Updating to the new blessing only exacerbates an issue that had us avoiding combat until we could hedgespin armor for everybody else. Not because we couldn't win fights, but because there was no way to make an encounter that was threatening for me but not lethal for everyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T17:34:02-07:00","id":496897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=496840#post496840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not because we couldn't win fights, but because there was no way to make an encounter that was threatening for me but not lethal for everyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why does a scene have to be threatening to all characters? If a scene involves disarming a bomb before a timer goes off, a character with high traits like Computer would not be even remotely as at-risk as characters lacking those abilities. I'm not sure why all given characters should be threatened by the same problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T18:05:21-07:00","id":496931,"title":"","content":"When I read how kiths were divorced from seemings, I was a little skeptical. Now, though, I love the idea. I'm so excited to play now!<br /> <br /> I kinda hope that we get examples of all the seemings with all the kiths. I suck at that sort of visual imagining, and i really love the idea of a Fairest Antiquarian, patiently explaing the details of a collection to a confused Keeper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5842-paladin742","name":"Paladin742","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T18:09:50-07:00","id":496934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=496897#post496897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why does a scene have to be threatening to all characters? If a scene involves disarming a bomb before a timer goes off, a character with high traits like Computer would not be even remotely as at-risk as characters lacking those abilities. I'm not sure why all given characters should be threatened by the same problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's more of a thing that it just makes the combat boring because the character that's not threatened by it can solve all your problems. But if it's threatening to the armour-heavy character, it'll straight out obliterate the armour-light characters unless the opponent completely ignores them...which can certainly strain the immersion of the game.<br /> <br /> WoD Combat is so all-consuming when it is in play that unless the confrontation gives something along the side (the new combat framing rules help!) for the squishier characters to do, they'll just get bored or frustrated as players.<br /> <br /> Narratively, there's usually a way to set up an encounter that has multiple goals, but sometimes there's just a straight up fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1462,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","user":"Xenesis","date":". 04-29-2015, 09:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T18:30:30-07:00","id":496941,"title":"","content":"I found some kiths that I considered boring or underwhelming in 1e are now interesting to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T19:01:51-07:00","id":496958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=496934#post496934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's more of a thing that it just makes the combat boring because the character that's not threatened by it can solve all your problems. But if it's threatening to the armour-heavy character, it'll straight out obliterate the armour-light characters unless the opponent completely ignores them...which can certainly strain the immersion of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. I guess I've never had that experience. The one fighty character in the team will sometimes go, &quot;You guys stay back. I've got this one,&quot; if there's something that'll threaten the rest of the team, but that she can handle just fine. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=496934#post496934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Narratively, there's usually a way to set up an encounter that has multiple goals, but sometimes there's just a straight up fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also never really have that experience. When there's just a straight-up fight, it's usually only involving specific characters. I never really have a situation where the entire crew just decides to get into a fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T19:16:55-07:00","id":496964,"title":"","content":"Xenesis pretty much nailed it. I'm not saying challenges shouldn't be easier for some characters than others, or that everyone should be equally involved in every single scene, because that obviously defeats the purpose of characters with different skill sets, but generally speaking my experience is that its boring and not fun when characters in the same party are so vastly discrepant in skill that character A has almost no chance to fail and character B has almost no chance to succeed. Bear in mind that this was a character with fairly unremarkable combat skills in other respects. 5 defense and 5 attack dice, actually lower than some other members of the party, but because of the armor I could get chomped on by a briar wolf the size of a truck while the rest of the party stayed out of range and waited for me to beat it to death. <br /> Yes, this problem can be avoided by having other objectives than &quot;kill the enemy and don't die&quot;, and/or by having a party that's more balanced in regard to combat aptitude, but armor is *disproportionately* good at making a character into a combat powerhouse for whom fights are trivial and therefore boring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T19:41:58-07:00","id":496979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=496958#post496958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hm. I guess I've never had that experience. The one fighty character in the team will sometimes go, &quot;You guys stay back. I've got this one,&quot; if there's something that'll threaten the rest of the team, but that she can handle just fine.<br /> <br /> I also never really have that experience. When there's just a straight-up fight, it's usually only involving specific characters. I never really have a situation where the entire crew just decides to get into a fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though it's a Hunter game, my group mostly has all members involved at once. Occasionally there are solo fights, but it's not really the norm, imho. We had a player who liked to sit out, but that actually kind of ruined the vibe/immersion for everyone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T19:56:44-07:00","id":497014,"title":"","content":"The longest Changeling the Lost game I played in, my character was a pacifist Wizened toymaker. During combats, while the crazy fire-sheathed sword dancer and the other members of the group fought, my character would pull injured people off of the field, get bystanders out of harm's way, find non-fighting ways to turn the tide or bring the combat to an end, etc. I never felt bored. I think part of the issue may be that a lot of folks go into &quot;tactical mode&quot; when combat breaks out in a game and stop role-playing their character and start treating things like a war game. Not trying to be critical of folks (I do it a lot myself, particularly in games that are combat-heavy) but I think a lot of the problem can be fixed by just thinking &quot;what would my character do in this situation&quot;? Also, from a Storyteller perspective, non-combatants are the best sort of leverage against combat powerhouses. You don't fight Superman directly, you go after his friends. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T20:09:13-07:00","id":497021,"title":"","content":"well in my case I think the problem was the player, and me as a novice GM (this was my 3rd session GMing and maybe 8th attempt ever). I think that having your character sit on the hill in a park playing on her computer, whilst the True Fae and the Gauru werewolf duke it out because you don't like combat is pretty immersion breaking. Now if players are enjoying not directly engaging but still participating (e.g. pulling people off the field or something) that'd be fine.<br /> <br /> Re: Kiths, like what I see so far (but I did a lot of skimming), any chance there'll be some sort of bug kith? I noticed a hive mind thing, I keep wanting to do a whole Zerg/'nid/Xenomorph horror like thing, so maybe it'll be doable?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T20:36:47-07:00","id":497037,"title":"","content":"I think you can definitely have parties with differing strength members, you just have to be careful. Few people enjoy doing nothing in a scene, so it's a good idea to find things that everyone can do. Think about the justice league, while Superman beats up Doomsday, Batman's disabling Luthor's space laser and Green Lantern is holding off Braniac's robot army with a giant shield. In a similar scenario you've got the Ogre is fighting the hobgoblin, the wizened is trying to find a way to close the hedge portal while the Fairest is distracting the cops. Obviously the hobgoblin is going to have to be strong enough to be a good fight for the Ogre, and yes that means that if he got around the Ogre he would likely be able to smash the Wizened or Fairest into a fine paste, that's why the Ogre is there to stop him, just like Doomsday is fairly matched by Superman but would squish Batman, they have different roles in the battle.<br /> <br /> I do feel that world of darkness combats are harder to structure as easily, especially when you go into it from a balance mentality. The simple fact is that not everyone builds combat focused characters. Thus the answer isn't to make the combats easier for these weaker characters, that just makes the characters who made fighting characters to feel bored. Give a fighting challenge to the fighter, a mental puzzle for the thinker, and a social encounter for the socialite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5823-ravian3","name":"Ravian3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T20:58:19-07:00","id":497045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=497021#post497021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that having your character sit on the hill in a park playing on her computer, whilst the True Fae and the Gauru werewolf duke it out because you don't like combat is pretty immersion breaking. Now if players are enjoying not directly engaging but still participating (e.g. pulling people off the field or something) that'd be fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I'm of a mind that Leverage is pretty much an ideal example of most RPG parties. So that's probably why my experience differs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T21:48:24-07:00","id":497087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravian3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=497037#post497037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you can definitely have parties with differing strength members, you just have to be careful. Few people enjoy doing nothing in a scene, so it's a good idea to find things that everyone can do. Think about the justice league, while Superman beats up Doomsday, Batman's disabling Luthor's space laser and Green Lantern is holding off Braniac's robot army with a giant shield. In a similar scenario you've got the Ogre is fighting the hobgoblin, the wizened is trying to find a way to close the hedge portal while the Fairest is distracting the cops. Obviously the hobgoblin is going to have to be strong enough to be a good fight for the Ogre, and yes that means that if he got around the Ogre he would likely be able to smash the Wizened or Fairest into a fine paste, that's why the Ogre is there to stop him, just like Doomsday is fairly matched by Superman but would squish Batman, they have different roles in the battle.<br /> <br /> I do feel that world of darkness combats are harder to structure as easily, especially when you go into it from a balance mentality. The simple fact is that not everyone builds combat focused characters. Thus the answer isn't to make the combats easier for these weaker characters, that just makes the characters who made fighting characters to feel bored. Give a fighting challenge to the fighter, a mental puzzle for the thinker, and a social encounter for the socialite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lot of truth in here.<br /> <br /> The key feature to remember is that the bad guys aren't going to fight you if they don't have something to lose, it's easier to retreat and just focus on losing you than try and kill you. So, fight-no, <i>action </i>scenes usually don't just have a brawl, but they have something going that also needs attention.<br /> <br /> The Huntsmen has the princess in the back of his car, but she's slipped out and is fighting against the guy in the back seat. Her fellow escapee and thug is shooting from the car behind him, and the driver has to dodge traffic and alternatively give the thug cover and clear lines of shot, all the while the engineer is trying to remove the bomb from their car before it goes.<br /> <br /> (Actual Play Example)The Kingmaker's Blade has been thrown and stuck into the branch hanging over the pit, and John Call the Canary is running to change into his monstrous bird shape with the kid sister on his back, leaving his flunkies to slow them all down. Stormy the Cat's gotta chase down the Canary and settle her affair with the asshole once and for all before he can get his wings under him, and Watcher's has no choice but to trust her on that since he's the only one who can reach Claimoh Solais before the loyalists do. This leaves Chun to trick the briarwolves onto his spearso they don't interrupt the other two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T22:30:21-07:00","id":497102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravian3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=497037#post497037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do feel that world of darkness combats are harder to structure as easily, especially when you go into it from a balance mentality. The simple fact is that not everyone builds combat focused characters. Thus the answer isn't to make the combats easier for these weaker characters, that just makes the characters who made fighting characters to feel bored. Give a fighting challenge to the fighter, a mental puzzle for the thinker, and a social encounter for the socialite.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I don't generally have a problem with that (and I try to do my best to achieve it when I'm storytelling), it's getting kind of far off from the original point - two modestly combat oriented characters will have vastly different experiences when one of them has swathes of free armour over the other. Armour has such an enormous, enormous effect on how deadly something is to a character I think that it is worth keeping it in mind.<br /> <br /> The 2.0 armour rules that specify coverage make this better, but I'm leery of a wyrd scaled armour that is full coverage, offers ranged plus melee protection and is sans defence, initiative and other penalties that would accompany actually wearing the physical clothing that would grant something of that magnitude (by virtue of omission rather than explicit wording, I guess).<br /> <br /> I'm not usually one to worry too much about fine grained balance and I don't really want to get into long drawn out discussions (that's not really the point of the thread) but it's something that I feel will cause problems at the tables of players, as I've had experiences where the sheer untouchableness of a character (PC or NPC) has led to a less than enjoyable experience for all those involved. It's not an issue of fairness so much as...frustration and boredom.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=497045#post497045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See, I'm of a mind that Leverage is pretty much an ideal example of most RPG parties. So that's probably why my experience differs.</div> </div> </div> </div>As much as I love Leverage, sometimes everyone wants to be Elliott. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1462,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","user":"Xenesis","date":".  Clarity 04-30-2015, 01:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T23:07:44-07:00","id":497126,"title":"","content":"I really liked the quote for Artist on first impression... The Gravewright also struck me... The quote pulled me in and wow, their blessing is powerful! I can see them being the bit of envy or ire of a Sin-Eater, the thing can <i>spend glamour to wipe away or give out an Anchor!</i> It's a tempting kith to play if easy access to the Underworld happens. Playing as Greys is a fun little add, I liked that.<br /> <br /> The Illes has always been one of my faves, glad to see it's still going to be around. I loved it's write-up, the Darkling and Ogre appearances are great for different reasons. The Maker along with other kiths (such as the Grey) gave me a real Eclipse Phase feel, of the whole autonomists living in prideful rebellion of the corporations... Here it'd be the Keepers, but I'm seeing a bit more bravado of '<i>I've survived and I'm here and you ain't gonna get me again</i>' element to Changeling now.<br /> <br /> I'm also getting a kinda Heist feel from some of their quotes too... Seems like it's mentioned before now with Leverage though! xD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T23:30:34-07:00","id":497133,"title":"","content":"I find it odd that Draconics get Wyrd lethal to bashing, lethal unarmed and for 1 glamor get Wyrd armor <i>instead</i> of lethal -&gt; bashing, but Metalflesh get Stamina armor and then <i>add</i> Wyrd lethal -&gt; bashing for 1 glamor.<br /> <br /> I think it would be more interesting if instead of gaining the armor Draconics received the most iconic of dragon attacks: the Breath Weapon, one that does lethal damage in a short cone in front of the Draconic and useable every 11-Wyrd rounds, or 6-Resovle rounds, or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T01:06:50-07:00","id":497215,"title":"","content":"&quot;We're True Fae. There wasn't exactly a committee.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T02:37:12-07:00","id":497254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=497133#post497133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it odd that Draconics get Wyrd lethal to bashing, lethal unarmed and for 1 glamor get Wyrd armor <i>instead</i> of lethal -&gt; bashing, but Metalflesh get Stamina armor and then <i>add</i> Wyrd lethal -&gt; bashing for 1 glamor.<br /> <br /> I think it would be more interesting if instead of gaining the armor Draconics received the most iconic of dragon attacks: the Breath Weapon, one that does lethal damage in a short cone in front of the Draconic and useable every 11-Wyrd rounds, or 6-Resovle rounds, or something.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> balancing something around cooldowns seems a bad idea to me. Just have a glamour cost on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T03:53:08-07:00","id":497293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=497133#post497133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it would be more interesting if instead of gaining the armor Draconics received the most iconic of dragon attacks: the Breath Weapon, one that does lethal damage in a short cone in front of the Draconic and useable every 11-Wyrd rounds, or 6-Resovle rounds, or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno. The Draconic as presented here is the Dragon-as-ruler, not the dragon-as-destroyer. The Ifrit kith will be great at representing dragons of fire, and I'm certain Venombite will be able to represent the venomous ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T04:15:03-07:00","id":497306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=496109#post496109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh! Yes. They'd count. So our Ifrit could pick up some of the Psychokinesis Merits from Hurt Locker, theoretically. I'll make that clearer. This would bypass some of the normal limitations on Supernatural Merits.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thanks for the quick answer, and that opens up some pretty cool options. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Are multiple seemings going to be a thing, either along the lines of a merit or a wyrd evolution? I can't see multi-kith changelings working in the new narrative without working vacations back to Arcadia or very pricy haggling in a goblin market.<br /> <br /> But narratively speaking, a changeling deciding their life is going to be a tale of beauty and power, I could see that. Presuming the seemings don't give bonuses that would make that overpowered. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T05:01:15-07:00","id":497323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=497306#post497306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for the quick answer, and that opens up some pretty cool options. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Are multiple seemings going to be a thing, either along the lines of a merit or a wyrd evolution? I can't see multi-kith changelings working in the new narrative without working vacations back to Arcadia or very pricy haggling in a goblin market.<br /> <br /> But narratively speaking, a changeling deciding their life is going to be a tale of beauty and power, I could see that. Presuming the seemings don't give bonuses that would make that overpowered.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure. I need to feel the game as it stands before I grow it out from there, you know? If it feels right in testing, I might go that route.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T05:10:21-07:00","id":497328,"title":"","content":"Multiple kiths strikes me as something that works at character generation, at least. The Chimera bit implies the Fae try to mash up kiths on occasion. It has to work some of the time, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T07:48:36-07:00","id":497443,"title":"","content":"do seemings still get bonuses to stats (like Fairest to presence and such), or is that handled strictly via contracts and kith blessings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T08:30:04-07:00","id":497462,"title":"","content":"Mostly, I'm blown away at the size of it. I'll need to take the time to read it over at a later time. Right now, however? A few words of something that struck me at a quick glance through, then to class!<br /> <br /> The Brollachan feels like its the new Darkling. Or, at least, it represents the skulking, scary thing in the shadows that the Darklings did in 1e, with the way things are different now in 2e and Seemings meaning you escaped. Curious to see how everything will interact. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T09:03:06-07:00","id":497513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=497102#post497102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I don't generally have a problem with that (and I try to do my best to achieve it when I'm storytelling), it's getting kind of far off from the original point - two modestly combat oriented characters will have vastly different experiences when one of them has swathes of free armour over the other. Armour has such an enormous, enormous effect on how deadly something is to a character I think that it is worth keeping it in mind.<br /> <br /> The 2.0 armour rules that specify coverage make this better, but I'm leery of a wyrd scaled armour that is full coverage, offers ranged plus melee protection and is sans defence, initiative and other penalties that would accompany actually wearing the physical clothing that would grant something of that magnitude (by virtue of omission rather than explicit wording, I guess).<br /> <br /> I'm not usually one to worry too much about fine grained balance and I don't really want to get into long drawn out discussions (that's not really the point of the thread) but it's something that I feel will cause problems at the tables of players, as I've had experiences where the sheer untouchableness of a character (PC or NPC) has led to a less than enjoyable experience for all those involved. It's not an issue of fairness so much as...frustration and boredom.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As much as I love Leverage, sometimes everyone wants to be Elliott. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's still possible to balance different combat oriented characters. Going back to the Justice League example, Superman wasn't the only one who fought, everyone was quite capable of fighting, Supes just has the biggest guns. So think about everyone's capabilities, armor guy is going to be able to take much greater blows than other people, so give him something particularly big to fight off, meanwhile the others have a range of various combat skills, so give them some smaller guys. The Justice League equivalent is Superman fighting Darkseid, while the rest of the justice league fight various weaker minions of Apokolips. The Changeling example is a motley of Privateers have some hedgebeast on a chain for the big armored guy to fight.<br /> <br /> Essentially armor makes you the tank, you can take on much bigger enemies than regular changelings, but that generally means your primary job is to put yourself between them and your squishier friends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5823-ravian3","name":"Ravian3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T09:56:20-07:00","id":497582,"title":"","content":"Question (and sorry if it's been addressed somewhere that I didn't see): How do you expect a new player to wade through 100 Kiths and decide what she wants her character to be? I mean, in terms of starting player choice, this sounds like a daunting task\u2026<br /> <br /> I guess that\u2019s my biggest worry about this. In First Edition, the process of Kith-after-Seeming made those choices linear, and the fact that one of the Lost didn\u2019t NEED a Kith within his Seeming left a lot of options open in the character development process.<br /> <br /> My troupe adopted notions that Kith can \u2019emerge\u2019 later, that a \u2018fresh\u2019 changeling need time and effort to understand what all happened to her. The loss of pieces of her soul to the thorns (on the way into Arcadia and on the way back out) left bits and bobs that were replaced by the stuff of Faerie. The journey of discovering just WHAT that means, both in terms of game mechanics and in the character\u2019s mind, was a huge part of our enjoyment of <b>Changeling: the Lost</b>.<br /> <br /> This version appears to mandate (and please correct me if I\u2019m wrong) that a specific Kith be chosen for a new character like how a <b>Vampire: the Requiem</b> player chooses a Clan. <b>Vampire</b> has five Clans, but now <b>Changeling</b> has 100 Kiths, which is a hell of a big difference. Starting with a Seeming (one of six) wasn\u2019t a huge conceptual hurdle, and once Seeming\u2019s chosen, a Kith grows out of that.<br /> <br /> \u2026This is a concern, mind you, not a gripe. My troupe has evolved a very fluid notion of how Kith and Seeming interact, not unlike the one you\u2019re adding to Second Edition. The difference is that we\u2019ve studied and played and worked on the game for years. A new player won\u2019t have that advantage, will she? I just detest the idea of saying, \u2018Welcome to the game! Here\u2019s your homework.\u2019 :\\<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T10:22:09-07:00","id":497615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arlecchino</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=496102#post496102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I think the Greys fall outside that thematic frame. While I would agree cryptids and urban legends are modern folklore, working in aliens strikes me as too wild a departure from the timeless magical creatures Changeling otherwise draws from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their tone and blessing make them work pretty well as muses and spirit guides as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> We all know the Gentry can't create truly new things, only steal and copy - but these kiths make me wonder if they're capable of anything at all without humans to work through (barring abduction; I guess they're pretty good at that) - or if they barely even <i>exist</i> without their victims. Don't get me wrong, I mean that as a compliment - it provides an interesting atmosphere.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T10:34:25-07:00","id":497625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phaolan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=497582#post497582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Question (and sorry if it's been addressed somewhere that I didn't see): How do you expect a new player to wade through 100 Kiths and decide what she wants her character to be? I mean, in terms of starting player choice, this sounds like a daunting task\u2026<br /> <br /> I guess that\u2019s my biggest worry about this. In First Edition, the process of Kith-after-Seeming made those choices linear, and the fact that one of the Lost didn\u2019t NEED a Kith within his Seeming left a lot of options open in the character development process.<br /> <br /> My troupe adopted notions that Kith can \u2019emerge\u2019 later, that a \u2018fresh\u2019 changeling need time and effort to understand what all happened to her. The loss of pieces of her soul to the thorns (on the way into Arcadia and on the way back out) left bits and bobs that were replaced by the stuff of Faerie. The journey of discovering just WHAT that means, both in terms of game mechanics and in the character\u2019s mind, was a huge part of our enjoyment of <b>Changeling: the Lost</b>.<br /> <br /> This version appears to mandate (and please correct me if I\u2019m wrong) that a specific Kith be chosen for a new character like how a <b>Vampire: the Requiem</b> player chooses a Clan. <b>Vampire</b> has five Clans, but now <b>Changeling</b> has 100 Kiths, which is a hell of a big difference. Starting with a Seeming (one of six) wasn\u2019t a huge conceptual hurdle, and once Seeming\u2019s chosen, a Kith grows out of that.<br /> <br /> \u2026This is a concern, mind you, not a gripe. My troupe has evolved a very fluid notion of how Kith and Seeming interact, not unlike the one you\u2019re adding to Second Edition. The difference is that we\u2019ve studied and played and worked on the game for years. A new player won\u2019t have that advantage, will she? I just detest the idea of saying, \u2018Welcome to the game! Here\u2019s your homework.\u2019 :\\<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There are three strategies I can recommend:<br /> <br /> 1) Have an expert. One person who's reviewed all 100 in detail and is able to hear a character concept and say, &quot;Ah! Here are two kiths that sound similar.&quot; Now you only have to deal with 2 choices.<br /> <br /> 2) Skip the fluff and read the blessings. Your goal is to get a sense of power level. Then, when you have a character concept, just skip all the ones in the book and come up with one whole cloth.<br /> <br /> 3) Skip the kith, as you've been doing, and just have a character concept. Gain your blessing at some point later when you've got a handle on things. Or never, if it doesn't bother you to not have access to the extra bonus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T10:42:37-07:00","id":497628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=496375#post496375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this new approach to building powers that started in Werewolf and continues here, what with using existing mechanics rather than having to build native mechanics for each splat to do the same things.</div> </div> </div> </div>...I don't know that I agree. Oh, I DO recognise the expediency of not 'doubling up' on powers and mechanics that already exist, but I think that using an off-the-shelf approach really weakens the feeling of every 'splat' being unique. This could especially become an issue with any kind of cross-over game. I mean, if a changeling's kith is defined by her access to a Merit and a quick imposition of a Tilt, can't another creature meet that same set of criteria? Beyond that, I can see 'metagame' issues of players getting into the habit of saying, 'That dude's just given me a Condition, ain't no thang.'<br /> <br /> Please know that *I* know it's not exactly as I state above, but it's something that rubbed me wrong when I first saw this. I believe that I'll get over it (David's comment about the references to God-Machine Chronicle and other sources being eventually 'integrated' into the <b>Changeling</b> book means a LOT to me), and no one needs to take my comments too seriously. I'm just processing...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T11:04:15-07:00","id":497637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=497625#post497625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are three strategies I can recommend:</div> </div> </div> </div>I appreciate those, and let me address them (as they ARE things that I've considered):<br /> <br /> 1) <i>Have an expert.</i> This IS good advice, but it's not always possible for every group. Sometimes we're all newbies. Furthermore, it comes with the possibility (not a lock, mind you!) of pedagogery, a huge 'turn-off' for new players, at least in my experience.<br /> <br /> 2) <i>Skip the fluff and read the blessings.</i> This can work, but it also comes with issues of possibly pandering power gamers, possibly requiring no less amount of 'background study' to comprehend, and the same issues of players wondering just what have they agreed to do (something that DOES very much fit into the <i>feel</i> of <b>Changeling</b>, I know!).<br /> <br /> 3) <i>Skip the kith, as you've been doing, and just have a character concept.</i> I think THIS is what I'd be prone to do, actually...<br /> <br /> My recommendation to David and his team is to consider these points and possibly put some similar direction into the game's 'Character Creation' pages.<br /> <br /> Thanks so much <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216\">Errol216</a></b> for the ideas!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T11:24:57-07:00","id":497652,"title":"","content":"Yeah I'd generally recommend a mixture between 1 and 3. At the very least have someone read through and at least somewhat understand the kith list (most likely the storyteller since he can focus on helping all the players during character creation.) After you have someone understanding it, they can help people build by starting with character concept a move on from there. Generally the way I approached my players when building changelings is, &quot;This is a modern fairy tale setting, what kind of character do you want to play? I'm almost certain there's at least one way to make that work.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5823-ravian3","name":"Ravian3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T13:22:44-07:00","id":497799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phaolan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=497582#post497582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Question (and sorry if it's been addressed somewhere that I didn't see): How do you expect a new player to wade through 100 Kiths and decide what she wants her character to be? I mean, in terms of starting player choice, this sounds like a daunting task\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div> While there's a lot of them, we also seem to come to the point where we're talking about pretty unique things. So, we've got a character concept, don't we?<br /> <br /> &quot;I want to play a dragon!&quot; obviously goes with a certain kith. A djinn? A certain ice princess? They all have pretty clear equivalents.<br /> <br /> There may be 100 kiths, but they're all pretty stand alone concepts. I don't really see any overlap in our example 30, and there's lots of ideas left open. I think that, as long as you come with an idea of what you want to play, its pretty easy to scan through until you find the appropriate one. <br /> <br /> I think the bigger problem is that the sheer number could be intimidating. Some kind of chart or something might be handy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T16:32:26-07:00","id":497981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phaolan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=497637#post497637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I appreciate those, and let me address them (as they ARE things that I've considered):<br /> <br /> 1) <i>Have an expert.</i> This IS good advice, but it's not always possible for every group. Sometimes we're all newbies. Furthermore, it comes with the possibility (not a lock, mind you!) of pedagogery, a huge 'turn-off' for new players, at least in my experience.<br /> <br /> 2) <i>Skip the fluff and read the blessings.</i> This can work, but it also comes with issues of possibly pandering power gamers, possibly requiring no less amount of 'background study' to comprehend, and the same issues of players wondering just what have they agreed to do (something that DOES very much fit into the <i>feel</i> of <b>Changeling</b>, I know!).<br /> <br /> 3) <i>Skip the kith, as you've been doing, and just have a character concept.</i> I think THIS is what I'd be prone to do, actually...<br /> <br /> My recommendation to David and his team is to consider these points and possibly put some similar direction into the game's 'Character Creation' pages.<br /> <br /> Thanks so much <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216\">Errol216</a></b> for the ideas!</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. Additionally, players should be developing characters together. So certain Kiths are going to come out in that conversation. In my experience so far, it's led to more shared Durances, which has been awesome. <br /> <br /> Also, we've had little difficulty once we built Durances as part of character creation. When you realize your role, finding a Kith's cake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T17:27:37-07:00","id":498028,"title":"","content":"The descriptions of Nightsinger Fairest and Witchtooth Fairest look awfully similar, but maybe that's just me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2286-indarkestknight","name":"indarkestknight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T18:50:13-07:00","id":498088,"title":"","content":"Question, but about Seemings rather than kiths: Since your Seeming has to do with how you escaped/left Arcadia, what about the changelings that left with the consent of their keeper?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5775-periculum","name":"Periculum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T18:57:35-07:00","id":498091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Periculum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=498088#post498088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question, but about Seemings rather than kiths: Since your Seeming has to do with how you escaped/left Arcadia, what about the changelings that left with the consent of their keeper?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They've mentioned this before, not every changeling has a Seeming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T18:58:45-07:00","id":498094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Periculum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=498088#post498088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question, but about Seemings rather than kiths: Since your Seeming has to do with how you escaped/left Arcadia, what about the changelings that left with the consent of their keeper?</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't really get a Seeming. They didn't take control. They're pure Kith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T19:15:34-07:00","id":498112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=498094#post498094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't really get a Seeming. They didn't take control. They're pure Kith.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a tiny point of curiosity about those who left Arcadia without taking back their lives themselves. Is it possible for such Changelings to reclaim their agency and acquire a Seeming at some later point? I could see reasons for and against, but I'm curious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T20:11:46-07:00","id":498144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=498112#post498112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have a tiny point of curiosity about those who left Arcadia without taking back their lives themselves. Is it possible for such Changelings to reclaim their agency and acquire a Seeming at some later point? I could see reasons for and against, but I'm curious.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see it. I don't know if we'll address it in the core, but definitely in REDACTED.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T20:11:48-07:00","id":498145,"title":"","content":"Was talking with one of my players (hunters) about their escape from the city (since they started a war) and where they were going to go (since they're also fugitives from the law) and the discussion of sailing to south america came up. I realized that although I've got tons of land monsters, I don't seem to have as many sea monsters (not that land monsters can't sail).<br /> <br /> just went and fished through the sample (pun not intended but I'm leaving it), nix look like they'll do, but it'd be great if something about the hedge and keepers, etc, for them made it into the book so we've got more sea options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T20:36:45-07:00","id":498181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=498094#post498094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They don't really get a Seeming. They didn't take control. They're pure Kith.</div> </div> </div> </div> Speaking of which, I wonder how much being Seeming-less is putting a target on your head. I mean, if the majority of Loyalists go without....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T20:42:36-07:00","id":498214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=498181#post498181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Speaking of which, I wonder how much being Seeming-less is putting a target on your head. I mean, if the majority of Loyalists go without....</div> </div> </div> </div>Seeming, at least in the perception I currently have, is a much less concrete thing. Depending on your Kith, you could probably pass for a given Seeming without one. You might be a lacklustre example, but an example none the less. For example, if you're a Seeming-free Draconic, you might pretend to be a Beast with just some heavy behavior acting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T21:07:25-07:00","id":498254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=498145#post498145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was talking with one of my players (hunters) about their escape from the city (since they started a war) and where they were going to go (since they're also fugitives from the law) and the discussion of sailing to south america came up. I realized that although I've got tons of land monsters, I don't seem to have as many sea monsters (not that land monsters can't sail).<br /> <br /> just went and fished through the sample (pun not intended but I'm leaving it), nix look like they'll do, but it'd be great if something about the hedge and keepers, etc, for them made it into the book so we've got more sea options.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well 1e had four kiths to do with water. They were the Swimmerskin (Beast's natural water dwellers), Nix (the mermaid Beast type), Waterborn and Water-dweller. There's some overlap between them, though Waterborn are more speedy natural water-dwellers and Waterborn are those water demons adept to looking through murky depths. The Swimmerskin has the ability to cross between water and land easier than a Waterborn, though it's not as fast as they are. I can see that a Swimmerskin and Waterborn could possibly be crunched down into one kith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T21:12:48-07:00","id":498256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=498214#post498214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seeming, at least in the perception I currently have, is a much less concrete thing. Depending on your Kith, you could probably pass for a given Seeming without one. You might be a lacklustre example, but an example none the less. For example, if you're a Seeming-free Draconic, you might pretend to be a Beast with just some heavy behavior acting.</div> </div> </div> </div>This actually sort of answers the question I had about Kith overlap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T21:42:48-07:00","id":498278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=498214#post498214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seeming, at least in the perception I currently have, is a much less concrete thing. Depending on your Kith, you could probably pass for a given Seeming without one. You might be a lacklustre example, but an example none the less. For example, if you're a Seeming-free Draconic, you might pretend to be a Beast with just some heavy behavior acting.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does feel like it could be tricky to infer at a glance what parts of a Changeling come from her Seeming, what parts from her Kith, and what parts from other relatively superficial changes her Keeper induced. Like the example of the Keeper who's big on living statues and animalistic humans: all would fit that aesthetic theme, but for some, the Kith's mechanics would reflect those inhuman shapes, while others would have the bestial or sculpted look in their appearances, even as that look is more-or-less incidental to the Kith's actual mechanics and what the Changeling actually did there.<br /> <br /> You could conceivably have three Changelings who are beautiful tiger-people made of fire, and have a hard time picking out which one is a) the Elemental &lt;insert &quot;professionally good-looking&quot; Kith&gt; whose Keeper really liked animal people, b) the Beast Fireheart whose Keeper insisted on beauty in all her &quot;guests,&quot; or c) the simply very beautiful, Seeming-less Skogskra whose Keeper just couldn't get enough of everything appearing to be on fire.<br /> <br /> If it's anything like 1e, each Changeling will also get at least one free extra specialty to reflect quirks of their fey bodies smaller than the Kith blessing. e.g. an animalistic Kith that doesn't focus on heightened senses (or Beasts or incidentally animal-like Changelings, for that matter) could use that extra specialty or two to reflect the improved hearing and/or vision. Obviously, these specialties aren't as impressive as a 2e Kith blessing, but between that and Merits, some Changelings could &quot;fake it&quot; or be mistaken for something other than they are without much trouble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T01:03:42-07:00","id":498487,"title":"","content":"In werewolf the extra speciality they got morphed into an entire dot, so who knows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T02:00:57-07:00","id":498503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=498487#post498487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In werewolf the extra speciality they got morphed into an entire dot, so who knows.</div> </div> </div> </div>As of now, we don't have anything like that. If people are interested in seeing it, I'm not against the idea. I don't think I'd do a Specialty, though. I've always found adding Specialties to be really superficial. It's typically a Specialty the character concept should have anyway, so why not just add a general Specialty? Like with Hunter, you get a Specialty in an Asset Skill at creation. But like, I don't think I've ever seen a character NOT get a Specialty in those Skills without the designation of Asset Skills, so it's functionally identical to just adding an additional Specialty. <br /> <br /> I considered a Resistance or Finesse Attribute. Not sure though. Not given it much thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T05:21:18-07:00","id":498693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=498254#post498254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well 1e had four kiths to do with water. They were the Swimmerskin (Beast's natural water dwellers), Nix (the mermaid Beast type), Waterborn and Water-dweller. There's some overlap between them, though Waterborn are more speedy natural water-dwellers and Waterborn are those water demons adept to looking through murky depths. The Swimmerskin has the ability to cross between water and land easier than a Waterborn, though it's not as fast as they are. I can see that a Swimmerskin and Waterborn could possibly be crunched down into one kith.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's cool, I think right now I'm trying to look at things that might actually choose to currently live in the water. also would be interesting to have talk about an oceanic hedge. The problem I'm seeing stem's from all the splats fundamentally wearing a human skin, which is fine, but it's kind of lead to a lack of horrors of the deep, imho. Of course I might be missing something because I never really got into Changeling 1e (have it, read it at least once a long time ago). I'm just looking at Beast and Changeling as potential area's to get more coverage on this, since it may potentially come up in my group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T08:02:49-07:00","id":498837,"title":"","content":"1e Changeling in particular seems to feel like the Specialties are the best thing ever. One not-particularly-niche specialty was the entire benefit of an entitlement, and the Wyrdskill merit seems to be under the impression that a few free specialties is worth a 5 dot merit and an increase of the xp costs for a significant chunk of skills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T08:45:18-07:00","id":498923,"title":"","content":"Wyrdskill was just poor economics. Even if specialities were as hot as they seemed to think it would still have been way cheaper to just <i>buy them.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T10:23:44-07:00","id":499085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=498693#post498693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's cool, I think right now I'm trying to look at things that might actually choose to currently live in the water. also would be interesting to have talk about an oceanic hedge. The problem I'm seeing stem's from all the splats fundamentally wearing a human skin, which is fine, but it's kind of lead to a lack of horrors of the deep, imho. Of course I might be missing something because I never really got into Changeling 1e (have it, read it at least once a long time ago). I'm just looking at Beast and Changeling as potential area's to get more coverage on this, since it may potentially come up in my group.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> One of the big problems here is that while sea horrors can be interesting, the concept still leaves itself as a niche. That's one of the reason so many aquatic kiths ended up redundant<br /> <br /> Essentially all of them ended up doing the same thing to different degrees of effect. (Waterborn can breathe water and swim well for a scene with a point of glamour, but can't leave the water for that scene. Swimmerskins can hold their breath for 30 minutes and swim well for no cost. Waterdwellers can also hold their breath for thirty minutes but instead can see well underwater instead of swimming well.) When you get down to it Swimmerskins seem the best at what they did, while everything else was a way to play the same concept as a different seeming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5823-ravian3","name":"Ravian3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T13:14:48-07:00","id":499303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=496814#post496814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of the Gravewight blessing, another note: Reaching isn't a thing for non-spirit ephemeral beings, seeing as it's specifically a way to operate through the Gauntlet, and thus should probably not be on the list of Conditions the changeling can add or subtract. Relatedly, Materialized applies to the ghost, and thus should probably not be on the list of Conditions if the Gravewight's target is the thing supporting the ghost's manifestation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am also of the mind that the Gravewight's choices of Conditions should be limited to Ghosts. It would seem odd for them to create Open Conditions for Angels or Spirits.<br /> <br /> I also echo previous statements about the Razorhand and Aggravated damage. It doesn't match the design previous games are enforcing in terms of difficulty to achieve said forms of damage. Increasing the cost or creating more stipulations could help with this, or have it cause more Lethal damage using dice tricks or other modifiers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T13:23:38-07:00","id":499308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GilboD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=499303#post499303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am also of the mind that the Gravewight's choices of Conditions should be limited to Ghosts. It would seem odd for them to create Open Conditions for Angels or Spirits.<br /> <br /> I also echo previous statements about the Razorhand and Aggravated damage. It doesn't match the design previous games are enforcing in terms of difficulty to achieve said forms of damage. Increasing the cost or creating more stipulations could help with this, or have it cause more Lethal damage using dice tricks or other modifiers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with both of these. For Razorhands, something like 8-again on attacks with their natural weapon for the scene would be nasty. They don't hit more often but they do lots of damage when they do from knowing where to hit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T13:49:16-07:00","id":499357,"title":"","content":"Talking about Chimera with my wife, we both agreed we weren't entirely happy with the write-up, but we came upon the idea of it being two or more people put together into one body (of whatever sort). The Blessing could give them bonuses to mental actions where having more than one mind might benefit (like remembering things) or give them added resistance to mental manipulation (again, because more than one mind is brought to bear). I was just tickled by the concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T13:57:45-07:00","id":499366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=499357#post499357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Talking about Chimera with my wife, we both agreed we weren't entirely happy with the write-up, but we came upon the idea of it being two or more people put together into one body (of whatever sort). The Blessing could give them bonuses to mental actions where having more than one mind might benefit (like remembering things) or give them added resistance to mental manipulation (again, because more than one mind is brought to bear). I was just tickled by the concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually liked the idea behind the Chimera kith in the draft, even if I thought the mechanical implementation of the blessing was a little out of sorts. That sounds cool too though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T15:58:52-07:00","id":499465,"title":"","content":"I love the way Kiths work overall now. They really have some <i>oomph</i> to them. Especially Windwings, which were probably always my favorite. Love 'em a lot more now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Claire C. \u2022 <b>Gaea Games Developer </b>\u2022 <b>Onyx Path Freelancer</b> (a.k.a. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield\" target=\"_blank\">Claire Redfield</a>)<br /> Now on Kickstarter: <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/1027237145/city-of-the-dead\" target=\"_blank\"><b>City of the Dead</b></a>, my survival horror roleplaying game introducing the GAEA System. COTD includes special emphasis on building and rebuilding communities, mental and social abilitiies.<br /> Twitter: <a href=\"https://twitter.com/GaeaGames\" target=\"_blank\">@GaeaGames</a> \u2022 Patreon: <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/GaeaGames\" target=\"_blank\">GaeaGames</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5822-gaea-games","name":"Gaea Games","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5822_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T17:53:43-07:00","id":499558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaea Games</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=499465#post499465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the way Kiths work overall now. They really have some <i>oomph</i> to them. Especially Windwings, which were probably always my favorite. Love 'em a lot more now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad that NWOD2.0 finally dispensed with the incredibly severe fear of allowing supernaturals to fly that 1.0 had.<br /> <br /> It'll be nice to have flying kith that can actually fly rather than just sort of awkwardly glide or fall really slowly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T19:01:29-07:00","id":499644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=499558#post499558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm glad that NWOD2.0 finally dispensed with the incredibly severe fear of allowing supernaturals to fly that 1.0 had.<br /> <br /> It'll be nice to have flying kith that can actually fly rather than just sort of awkwardly glide or fall really slowly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I got the okay to do this, so...enjoy!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Windwing</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Courier, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">They gave me a new freedom so they could take it away. Now nothing is ever taking it from me. I will never be close enough to the ground for jealous hands to touch me.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Windwings are most often found in the habitats of Keepers that don\u2019t bother dividing the land and sky, or in realms with immeasurably tall features. These changelings are hollowed out by their Keepers and stretched thin. A painful process, but nothing compared to being earthbound by the transition through the Hedge. Some Windwings regret escaping their masters, but few who return find the skies of Arcadia as freeing as they remember.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">\u2022 </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Beast:</b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Agile, feathered and narrow, with scaled feet and long noses or beaks. Graceful in a way few things will ever manage to be.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">\u2022 </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Darkling:</b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Leaf-nosed with red eyes and bat-like ears. They have teeth too large and claws at the end of their wings.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">\u2022</span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Elemental: </b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Transparent except for the clouds beneath their skin. Puffy and white when they\u2019re pleased, but grey and stormy when they\u2019re not.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Blessing:</b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> The Windwing can fly at (Speed+2) for as many turns as they have dots in Stamina, but must spend a turn without a movement action before they can fly again. They can spend a Glamour to increase the duration of their flight for a minute per Wyrd or until they land, whichever is shorter. During their flight, they can use their Defense against Firearms. Windwings count as Size 2 for the purposes of perching on objects that shouldn\u2019t be capable of holding their weight.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Claire C. \u2022 <b>Gaea Games Developer </b>\u2022 <b>Onyx Path Freelancer</b> (a.k.a. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield\" target=\"_blank\">Claire Redfield</a>)<br /> Now on Kickstarter: <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/1027237145/city-of-the-dead\" target=\"_blank\"><b>City of the Dead</b></a>, my survival horror roleplaying game introducing the GAEA System. COTD includes special emphasis on building and rebuilding communities, mental and social abilitiies.<br /> Twitter: <a href=\"https://twitter.com/GaeaGames\" target=\"_blank\">@GaeaGames</a> \u2022 Patreon: <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/GaeaGames\" target=\"_blank\">GaeaGames</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5822-gaea-games","name":"Gaea Games","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5822_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T20:34:39-07:00","id":499713,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Eee. This makes me really happy.<br /> <br /> Actual flight! (And the defence vs. firearms means that you'll actually want to fly in a fight, too!)<br /> <br /> </span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ifrit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Blessing: </b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">They gain the 8-again quality to all Intimidation rolls. If they spend a point of Glamour, they can use the three-dot Psychokinesis Merit (God Machine Chronicles, pp. 173-174) to affect fire for one scene and without the need to spend Willpower. Manipulating fire in an obvious fashion also adds +2 dice to all of their Intimidation rolls. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><br /> Considering the more malleable nature of the new kiths and seemings - is there any real reason to just limit this to pyrokinesis?</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T20:49:43-07:00","id":499728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=499713#post499713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Eee. This makes me really happy.<br /> <br /> Actual flight! (And the defence vs. firearms means that you'll actually want to fly in a fight, too!)<br /> <br /> <br /> Considering the more malleable nature of the new kiths and seemings - is there any real reason to just limit this to pyrokinesis?</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Based on what's been said it sounds like elemental reskinning will be encouraged.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T23:18:38-07:00","id":499885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravian3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=499085#post499085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Essentially all of them ended up doing the same thing to different degrees of effect. (Waterborn can breathe water and swim well for a scene with a point of glamour, but can't leave the water for that scene. Swimmerskins can hold their breath for 30 minutes and swim well for no cost. Waterdwellers can also hold their breath for thirty minutes but instead can see well underwater instead of swimming well.) When you get down to it Swimmerskins seem the best at what they did, while everything else was a way to play the same concept as a different seeming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed that it is fairly niche. I'm pretty glad we'll see a more aquatic based splat with Beast:the Primordial though, if only for my love of Deep Ones and Kappa. That kinda fell under the purview of the Water-Dweller in Changeling 1e (depth dwelling water demons).<br /> <br /> @ xenoterracide; If you want something more naturally lived in the water, that'll be the Waterborn as they can actually breath underwater rather than hold their breath. The difference between them with the Swimmerskin is that they also are able to swim at twice full speed, which takes the edge off choosing whether to breath normally in water and hold breath on air or vice-versa each scene. If you want to see the statblock for the Waterborn, they are an Elemental Kith that appears in the corebook.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Changelings who are imbued with the nature of the waters, soft and brutal, gentle and mighty: Undines and nymphs, man-eating river demons, water babies, ladies of the lake. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T00:04:04-07:00","id":499931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=499728#post499728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Based on what's been said it sounds like elemental reskinning will be encouraged.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, taking the example blessings and making new kiths based on them was mentioned in the excerpt.<br /> <br /> So you'd rather have photokinesis? You're kith Angel or Shining One.<br /> <br /> Electrokinesis? Stormling.<br /> <br /> Cryokinesis? Cold One.<br /> <br /> Or you know, whatever name seems cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T01:06:59-07:00","id":499983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=499885#post499885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If you want something more naturally lived in the water, that'll be the Waterborn as they can actually breath underwater rather than hold their breath. The difference between them with the Swimmerskin is that they also are able to swim at twice full speed, which takes the edge off choosing whether to breath normally in water and hold breath on air or vice-versa each scene. If you want to see the statblock for the Waterborn, they are an Elemental Kith that appears in the corebook.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well the biggest problem is that by the rules a Waterborn's ability only lasts for a scene an costs glamour to maintain. I'm not sure there's a definite limit to how long a scene can lasts but I'm guessing that they're probably not capable of living a fully aquatic lifestyle. Meanwhile the other two just have the benefit of being able to spend up to thirty minutes underwater at a time. Too put that in perspective whales typically can go for around ninety minutes without air, and dolphins (and most other aquatic mammals) generally only manage around 5 to 7 minutes underwater at a time. Really for all intents and purposes a Swimmerskin could live a fully aquatic lifestyle if they wanted to and probably be better at it than a lot of real aquatic animals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5823-ravian3","name":"Ravian3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T22:25:22-07:00","id":501374,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I can see your point now. I still feel the Swimmerskin and Waterborn could probably be consolidated into one kith. The Nix have their voice ability that sets them apart and Water-Dwellers have enhanced vision in the murky depths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T01:15:19-07:00","id":501487,"title":"","content":"So... I'm way too late to this discussion to really offer much, but I will say...<br /> <br /> I just love how much Blessings matter more from Kiths, and how their power upgrade really lets them fully live up to the concept they're supposed to embody.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T08:10:37-07:00","id":501710,"title":"","content":"So a quick random question.<br /> <br /> Will there be a Kith for charachters like Sleeping Beauty? Maybe something like people automatically assume you've innocent of any accusation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T10:50:28-07:00","id":501905,"title":"","content":"I'm having GSS flashbacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T10:59:07-07:00","id":501908,"title":"","content":"I think we need a succubus/incubbus kith, Besides the one of &quot;I'm pretty but only at night&quot;. Maybe one which give bonus on social rolls against the person he/she has seduced, similar to the Duchy of the Icebound Hearth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 05-03-2015, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T11:07:02-07:00","id":501910,"title":"","content":"Well, since the idea seems to be &quot;Revamp all the old kiths and bring in a sprinkling of new ones to round it out&quot;, I think that's very likely to happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T11:19:00-07:00","id":501937,"title":"","content":"Its been mentioned that the Romancer Kith ate the Succubus/Incubus Kith, Succubus is now the Darkling Romancer. It makes sense both are about seduction, Romancer is general purpose seductionist, Succubus is the Dark edge of seduction, the dangerous one.<br /> <br /> Given that Romancer is obviously about seduction and sex, a Darkling Romancer would be one who.used sex as a weapon of betrayal. <br /> <br /> I think Romancer Fairest will be like the God Cupid or Goddess Venus, Beast Romancers will be like Saytrs like Pan, and Darklings which are sexy with a demonic kinky edge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T11:19:51-07:00","id":501939,"title":"","content":"What's GSS?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T11:21:49-07:00","id":501941,"title":"","content":"I've suggested Romancer/Succubus kith could have striking looks merit and the ability to cause Wanton and Swoon conditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T11:29:26-07:00","id":501945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=501939#post501939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's GSS?</div> </div> </div> </div>Golden Sky Stories, a game where you play as animals(and other things) with small magical abilities who go around helping people and making friends. One of the powers that recur a lot is one where you can convince people that something wasn't your fault, which fit with a post that Raven had but seems to have taken down.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, I was just reminded of that power. It's a good one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T11:56:36-07:00","id":501960,"title":"","content":"You can't see that post any more? I still can?<br /> <br /> (This one right?)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=501710#post501710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a quick random question.<br /> <br /> Will there be a Kith for charachters like Sleeping Beauty? Maybe something like people automatically assume you've innocent of any accusation?</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T12:25:12-07:00","id":502001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=501960#post501960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't see that post any more? I still can?<br /> <br /> (This one right?)</div> </div> </div> </div>I can still see that one too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T14:28:37-07:00","id":502177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=501960#post501960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't see that post any more? I still can?<br /> <br /> (This one right?)<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I can see it now, I couldn't see it then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T14:31:57-07:00","id":502179,"title":"","content":"Okay, here's another question: Is it REALLY necessary to have examples for any Kith's Seeming mien?<br /> <br /> What I mean is, can't we just have a couple of lines for each Kith, offering common, shared physical traits (e.g. eyes, posture, size, skin tone), and THEN put into the Seeming write-ups common 'overlays' that these offer (e.g. elemental trappings, fur, striking auras, webs)? THEN you can maybe offer ideas in the 'character creation' section about how these things can come together (possibly adding in whatever Traits may come from Court affiliation and mantles).<br /> <br /> You kind of already have that under the 'Kith, Seeming and Appearance' heading, but it could be streamlined. Looking at the three Seemings shared so far, I see that the 'Appearance' bit is crazy-vague\u2014NOT a bad thing, mind you\u2014and leaves room for something more along the lines of commonalities. Beyond that, I dunno that it's really worth the space, time, and energy to give SOME examples for Seeming-specific miens in Kith descriptions when compared to the outcome for players.<br /> <br /> Here's an example of what I'm thinking: For the Draconic Kith mien, say something like, 'tends to share large size, intense\u2014if not outright fierce\u2014visages, and may include such things as scales, vestigial wings, or possibly claws.' For the Darkling Seeming, say maybe: 'Kith expresses as somehow diminished, sometimes fading into the shade of one's own shadow. Webs might adorn otherwise striking features, or dust and moths will shake out from every movement...' So in PLAY, going with the above example, our Draconic Darkling might have yellowed, burning eyes that appear to look out from pits burned into her face, and the clothes she wears flare into dark wings with cobweb tatters instead of skin.<br /> <br /> ...I dunno if I'm making my case very well, but the notion of giving us mix-and-match features rather than precise examples for miens strikes me as more open-ended. I know it might not jibe with the outline of Seeming coming before Kith in the book, but it's a notion.<br /> <br /> Just for the record, part of my issue with the idea of mien in general comes from the experience of creating characters for classic World of Darkness <b>Dark Ages: Fae</b>. The examples offered felt downright procrustean in their specificity, and I'd HATE to see <b>Changeling: the Lost</b> fall into that sort of possible mess. It also shaves word count off of the Kith writeups, but again, it might not be useful for this game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T17:38:51-07:00","id":502318,"title":"","content":"Examples aren't necessary, but they're often appreciated!<br /> <br /> I mean, otherwise you're assuming a huge amount of background knowledge from the player (in terms of lore/fluff) when building a character and a few worked examples really help streamline the character building process. Or they trigger the 'THAT SOUNDS AWESOME!' reflex in the brain and it gets adopted.<br /> <br /> While they're certainly using a chunk of wordcount, they're nice to have. And I'm sure if it really starts to eat into wordcount for what they want to introduce in that part, they'll shave off a few of the examples here and there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T18:03:43-07:00","id":502346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phaolan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=502179#post502179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, here's another question: Is it REALLY necessary to have examples for any Kith's Seeming mien?</div> </div> </div> </div>So far, most of my testers have specifically called them out as very useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T18:04:45-07:00","id":502349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=501710#post501710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a quick random question.<br /> <br /> Will there be a Kith for charachters like Sleeping Beauty? Maybe something like people automatically assume you've innocent of any accusation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a bad idea. I don't know if we currently have one, but I may be able to sneak one into Dark Eras if not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T20:44:12-07:00","id":502452,"title":"","content":"I absolutely love that the Kiths are no longer tied to a single Seeming! And I like the more potent blessings, too. I think this makes Kiths feel much more important to the character concept.<br /> <br /> I think, overall, the Kiths are feeling much more balanced than in 1e. Almost every Kith has some wow factor and feels worth playing with.<br /> <br /> However, I feel The Artist Kith blessing is a little lacking compared to a lot of the others. Getting easy exceptional successes on art is certainly cool, but it doesn't have a lot of utility aside from making art a little faster, selling it for more, or impressing art connoisseurs. Opportunities for this to be useful in games seem like they might be pretty limited, especially next to all the combat enhancing abilities and blessings that mimic psychic merits or grant unique and immediately useful powers. It would be awesome if their art could have some minor enchantment. Maybe when they create a piece of art and spend a Glamour during its creation they could choose a condition, and whenever someone experiences the art for the first time they gain that condition (addicted, broken, guilty, inspired, madness, spooked, obsession,and steadfast all seem like possibilities). This could be resisted by a Resolve or Composure and Wyrd roll. This would put them more on par with the Nightsinger. It would also be neat to have the endlessly toiling aspect from the Kith description represented by something in the blessing. Maybe 9 again on Stamina rolls to stay awake or being able to go a number of days without sleep equal to their Wyrd.<br /> <br /> I'm an artist myself, so I'm a bit biased. I actually decided to do a quick digital painting of what I imagine a Wizened Artist might look like. He's all head and arms. Long flexible neck. Extra joints in his fingers. Big eyes. His mouth is even adapted to holding brushes. Please check it out and let me know what you think: <a href=\"http://fav.me/d8ryhdr\" target=\"_blank\">http://fav.me/d8ryhdr</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T21:01:22-07:00","id":502460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=502452#post502452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, I feel The Artist Kith blessing is a little lacking compared to a lot of the others. Getting easy exceptional successes on art is certainly cool, but it doesn't have a lot of utility aside from making art a little faster, selling it for more, or impressing art connoisseurs. </div> </div> </div> </div>Exceptional successes provide Conditions. Conditions provide Beats. Beats help characters advance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T21:49:42-07:00","id":502484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=502460#post502460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exceptional successes provide Conditions. Conditions provide Beats. Beats help characters advance.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My bad. Haven't played very much with the updated rules yet, and hadn't considered the potential for Beats. So, the Artist Blessing is good for gaining positive conditions like Inspired or Steadfast, and/or for farming xp? That is definitely very beneficial. I guess it just seems a bit more mechanical, and less magical and immediately fun than having a power that can affect others' emotions like the Nightsinger or as useful and versatile as the Smith or Maker who are also really good at their chosen crafts, but can also repair/sabotage/modify items and do it in a reduced time (not to mention Smiths and Makers being focused on items that are more likely to come up in an average adventure).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T22:03:41-07:00","id":502514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=502484#post502484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> My bad. Haven't played very much with the updated rules yet, and hadn't considered the potential for Beats. So, the Artist Blessing is good for gaining positive conditions like Inspired or Steadfast, and/or for farming xp? That is definitely very beneficial. I guess it just seems a bit more mechanical, and less magical and immediately fun than having a power that can affect others' emotions like the Nightsinger or as useful and versatile as the Smith or Maker who are also really good at their chosen crafts, but can also repair/sabotage/modify items and do it in a reduced time (not to mention Smiths and Makers being focused on items that are more likely to come up in an average adventure).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you CAN farm XP with it. But, the whole thing about Conditions is, dramatic things have to happen for that XP to happen. So, artists are going to be proficient at creating dramatic situations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T22:55:52-07:00","id":502538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=502349#post502349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not a bad idea. I don't know if we currently have one, but I may be able to sneak one into Dark Eras if not.</div> </div> </div> </div> That would be awesome <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T08:35:07-07:00","id":502938,"title":"","content":"So, will there be a 2nd Water Kith? <br /> <br /> I'm sorry if this question got answered way upthread, and therefore, it's just annoying to hear it again, but, is there? Specifically thinking for someone or something that is essentially a living drop of water, for example(well, okay, bit bigger than a drop perhaps, but, you get the point.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T16:02:57-07:00","id":503579,"title":"","content":"There are four in 1st edition, so it's more than likely that some of these will be returning past the Nix, which was in the preview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T16:51:56-07:00","id":503625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=502514#post502514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, you CAN farm XP with it. But, the whole thing about Conditions is, dramatic things have to happen for that XP to happen. So, artists are going to be proficient at creating dramatic situations.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's a really interesting way of looking at it. Definitely gives one something to chew over.<br /> <br /> Hey, speaking of kiths that revolve around Conditions, so the official 2e name for the ghostly kith is Gravewright with an r? In the first edition corebook it's Gravewight, sans r, though other books occasionally spell it with. I know this is an extremely tiny thing, but for whatever reason it's burrowed itself into my head and laid eggs. Fortunately the name works either way, implying either an undead being who hangs around cemeteries, or someone who builds graves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T17:48:09-07:00","id":503656,"title":"","content":"[]<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=503625#post503625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a really interesting way of looking at it. Definitely gives one something to chew over.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm the author of the kiths David posted here, and I was initially a little worried about Artist being too weak, but the point of the kith is basically being an inhumanly good artist, and the bonus for spending Glamour, + needing only 3 successes for an Exceptional Success + creating Conditions accomplish this pretty darn well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hey, speaking of kiths that revolve around Conditions, so the official 2e name for the ghostly kith is Gravewright with an r? In the first edition corebook it's Gravewight, sans r, though other books occasionally spell it with. I know this is an extremely tiny thing, but for whatever reason it's burrowed itself into my head and laid eggs. Fortunately the name works either way, implying either an undead being who hangs around cemeteries, or someone who builds graves. </div> </div> </div>Very sadly, that was a typo on my part, in fact one of two errors on Gravewight - the other simply being that I didn't specify that they could only create and alter Conditions for ghosts. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/96-john-snead","name":"John Snead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar96_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T18:09:35-07:00","id":503696,"title":"","content":"If any of the 2e team are hanging around and willing to humor me, how about some favorites? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Of those we have and have not seen, which do you feel is...<br /> <br /> A) ... most improved Kith from 1e?<br /> B) ... best idea for a newcomer Kith?<br /> C) ... the Kith you'd least want to be?<br /> D) ... the Kith you'd most want to be?<br /> E) ... coolest Seeming-Kith example?<br /> F) ... personal favorite Kith of them all?<br /> <br /> We who've only seen the first third will just have to make do with what we've got.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T22:13:54-07:00","id":503825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John Snead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=503656#post503656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[] I'm the author of the kiths David posted here, and I was initially a little worried about Artist being too weak, but the point of the kith is basically being an inhumanly good artist, and the bonus for spending Glamour, + needing only 3 successes for an Exceptional Success + creating Conditions accomplish this pretty darn well.</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, awesome work on these kiths! Love 'em.<br /> <br /> I see where you guys are coming from with the Artist Kith now that I'm taking into account how Exceptional Successes generate Conditions/Beats in the new edition. However, I kind of wish that the Kith was more about creating inhumanly good art, instead of being an inhumanly good artist. As is, they are exceptional artists who can produce work much faster than usual. Presumably, they would also make really good art more consistently, though I don't think the rules explicitly state that. The art they create, however, is basically the same as that created by human artists. I think it would be awesome if, instead or in addition, they could make supernatural art - a play that drives people insane like the King in Yellow, hyper realistic paintings that instill deep horror in the viewer like in Pickman's Model, etc. I've been re-reading the Conditions section in GMC, and I'm thinking that they could possibly do this, to some extent, under the current rules. It says &quot;complex behaviors&quot; can cause Conditions; the example given is a well planned heist causing a police chief to be overwhelmed. So, conceivably, a well-executed work of art could instill Shaken (or something else appropriate) in viewers even though it's not explicitly stated in the rules. Would that be a correct reading of the rules? (I guess this would mean that even mortal artist's could do this; it would just be harder for them.)<br /> <br /> One final argument for adding a little something extra to the Artist's blessing:<br /> <br /> Now that I'm looking at the Artist a little differently, I compared it to other Kiths that are geared toward Exceptional Successes. The two that stood out were the Illes and the Palewraith.<br /> <br /> The Palewraith also needs only 3 for an Exceptional Success. <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It's true that they only gain that benefit under certain conditions, but those conditions are pretty easy to achieve. T</span></span></span>he Artist can spend Glamour for +3, yes, but Stealth is of much greater utility than making art in most games and is often rolled several times a scene when it's called for, whereas making art is an extended roll that could take minutes or even hours per roll and is normally relegated to pauses in the action. So, the Palewraith is arguably going to be getting a similar number of exceptional successes (and Conditions/Beats), or possibly more, give the greater frequency of their affected rolls. And, in addition to this, the Palewraith also gets a very useful combat ability (anything that gives you Defense against Firearms is pure gold).<br /> <br /> The Illes is actually even better at getting Exceptional Successes AND is focused in an area that will come up much more than creating art. Think about how often characters fast talk, seduce, entertain, and butter up NPCs in an average game. Nearly every game session will have a social scene (or several). Sure, the bonus is conditional, but the conditions aren't that hard to meet, and it can apply to a broad range of skills and applications. And when benefiting form the +4 and spending Glamour so that they only need 3 for an Exceptional Success, the Illes is MORE likely to gain an Exceptional Success than an Artist (assuming the same unmodified dice pool) because of the higher bonus to the rolls. <br /> <br /> So there are two Kiths with similar or even better potential for Exceptional Successes who also have abilities that are arguably more useful in an average story. And one of them also gets a sweet combat ability.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T22:42:31-07:00","id":503861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=503825#post503825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it would be awesome if, instead or in addition, they could make supernatural art - a play that drives people insane like the King in Yellow, hyper realistic paintings that instill deep horror in the viewer like in Pickman's Model, etc. I've been re-reading the Conditions section in GMC, and I'm thinking that they could possibly do this, to some extent, under the current rules. It says &quot;complex behaviors&quot; can cause Conditions; the example given is a well planned heist causing a police chief to be overwhelmed. So, conceivably, a well-executed work of art could instill Shaken (or something else appropriate) in viewers even though it's not explicitly stated in the rules. Would that be a correct reading of the rules? (I guess this would mean that even mortal artist's could do this; it would just be harder for them.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd just like to say, that this is a really, really sexy reading of the rules.<br /> <br /> I can imagine a whole bevy of artists, each with their own ideals and what they do with their art.<br /> <br /> A revolutionary militiaman that terrifies the officers of the state by creating battle standards that literally put the fear of the rebels into them.<br /> A punk street artist that draws the local homeless into safe places by creating inspiring graffiti that makes people feel safe and at ease.<br /> A political adversary that tries to bring people down by orating so well that people feel guilty about certain things.<br /> The classic paintings with eyes? :P<br /> <br /> I like this a lot.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T23:12:29-07:00","id":503870,"title":"","content":"Hmm, for clairity I might add a bit to the Artist Blessing: &quot;An Exceptional Success when creating art specifically allows them to create the Deprived, Guilty, Inspired, Shaken, Spooked, or Steadfast Condition in everyone who focuses on otherwise or partakes of this work of art. Even if not resolved, this Condition naturally fades a scene after someone leaves the presence of the work of art.&quot; <br /> <br /> Obviously, Deprived and Guilty in this case would both be applied very generally - almost everyone has something they obsess over or feel that they can't live without &amp; something they feel at least somewhat guilty about.<br /> <br /> As a side-note, after watching two seasons of <i>Hannibal</i>, I love the idea of an Artist who is a chef who creates food that inspires guilt, terror, or whatever in people who eat it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/96-john-snead","name":"John Snead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar96_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T00:13:12-07:00","id":503899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John Snead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=503870#post503870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, for clairity I might add a bit to the Artist Blessing: &quot;An Exceptional Success when creating art specifically allows them to create the Deprived, Guilty, Inspired, Shaken, Spooked, or Steadfast Condition in everyone who focuses on otherwise or partakes of this work of art. Even if not resolved, this Condition naturally fades a scene after someone leaves the presence of the work of art.&quot;<br /> <br /> Obviously, Deprived and Guilty in this case would both be applied very generally - almost everyone has something they obsess over or feel that they can't live without &amp; something they feel at least somewhat guilty about.<br /> <br /> As a side-note, after watching two seasons of <i>Hannibal</i>, I love the idea of an Artist who is a chef who creates food that inspires guilt, terror, or whatever in people who eat it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It may be a good idea to remind that exceptional success can impose conditions, but I don't think they should fade after a scene or be limited. Give the players a chance to be creative, if they can justify it to their Storyteller, its fair game!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T02:05:51-07:00","id":503993,"title":"","content":"A thought on Nightsinger and other kiths that might grant 8- or 9-again: they make the second dot of Professional Training much weaker. If your core concept is &quot;inhumanly good singer&quot; (for example) it's likely you'll take Profession(Singer) at some point.<br /> <br /> I don't know how big a deal that is, but it's something I can see coming up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T03:34:41-07:00","id":504021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=503993#post503993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A thought on Nightsinger and other kiths that might grant 8- or 9-again: they make the second dot of Professional Training much weaker. If your core concept is &quot;inhumanly good singer&quot; (for example) it's likely you'll take Profession(Singer) at some point.<br /> <br /> I don't know how big a deal that is, but it's something I can see coming up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. If I were running a campaign where this came up, I'd allow players to jump directly from 1 to 3 dots w/o having to purchase the 2nd dot.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/96-john-snead","name":"John Snead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar96_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T09:07:33-07:00","id":504231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaea Games</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=499644#post499644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I got the okay to do this, so...enjoy!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Windwing</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Courier, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">They gave me a new freedom so they could take it away. Now nothing is ever taking it from me. I will never be close enough to the ground for jealous hands to touch me.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Windwings are most often found in the habitats of Keepers that don\u2019t bother dividing the land and sky, or in realms with immeasurably tall features. These changelings are hollowed out by their Keepers and stretched thin. A painful process, but nothing compared to being earthbound by the transition through the Hedge. Some Windwings regret escaping their masters, but few who return find the skies of Arcadia as freeing as they remember.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">\u2022 </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Beast:</b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Agile, feathered and narrow, with scaled feet and long noses or beaks. Graceful in a way few things will ever manage to be.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">\u2022 </span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Darkling:</b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Leaf-nosed with red eyes and bat-like ears. They have teeth too large and claws at the end of their wings.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">\u2022</span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Elemental: </b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Transparent except for the clouds beneath their skin. Puffy and white when they\u2019re pleased, but grey and stormy when they\u2019re not.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Blessing:</b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> The Windwing can fly at (Speed+2) for as many turns as they have dots in Stamina, but must spend a turn without a movement action before they can fly again. They can spend a Glamour to increase the duration of their flight for a minute per Wyrd or until they land, whichever is shorter. During their flight, they can use their Defense against Firearms. Windwings count as Size 2 for the purposes of perching on objects that shouldn\u2019t be capable of holding their weight.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I really like this version of the Windwings. It does make me wonder, though, what happens to them when their duration of flight expires? Do they plummet to their death if they're out of Glamour and have flown a little too high, or do they get to fall or glide safely until they land?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T11:10:46-07:00","id":504389,"title":"","content":"Since the dual kith merit interested me before, I'm wondering if it's going to make a comeback. It looks to be a <i>much</i> bigger advantage this time, so I understand if it had to be cut.<br /> <br /> But Coyote was always my favored concept. Though I can easily see it having been replaced with a general purpose &quot;Trickster&quot; kith. (Hopefully one who's blessing actually deals with tricking people this time.)<br /> <br /> I think my fist character is likely to be a elementally-flavored-beast, or a beastly-looking-elemental...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T18:17:47-07:00","id":504906,"title":"","content":"This was from a while ago, but hey, touching back on it.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=498503#post498503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As of now, we don't have anything like [an extra specialty/dot]. If people are interested in seeing it, I'm not against the idea. I don't think I'd do a Specialty, though. I've always found adding Specialties to be really superficial. It's typically a Specialty the character concept should have anyway, so why not just add a general Specialty? Like with Hunter, you get a Specialty in an Asset Skill at creation. But like, I don't think I've ever seen a character NOT get a Specialty in those Skills without the designation of Asset Skills, so it's functionally identical to just adding an additional Specialty.<br /> <br /> I considered a Resistance or Finesse Attribute. Not sure though. Not given it much thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I'm basically in agreement that adding an extra Specialty really <i>is</i> pretty superficial, it's just a little something I've kinda liked for flavor reasons. I find the behavior you've seen interesting, as I tended to use it for little incidental changes the character experienced. Say, a Changeling gets out of the Hedge with hooves or horns for a Brawl specialty involving kicks or headbutts. I just find it fun to give those sorts of things some kind of mechanical reflection, should the character's Kith not cover them, even if they're not critical to the character concept. They don't really <i>need</i> anything, of course, but sometimes a Specialty is fun for a minor dash of flavor. By contrast, welcome as a Resistance/Finesse Attribute might be, it feels like it goes too large to scratch this (incredibly minor) itch. It's not like regular Specialties are exactly pricy, so it's hardly a big deal one way or the other.<br /> <br /> That said, you're right that there do have to be more interesting and substantive ways to reflect that sort of thing. At the least, taking a Merit or two and refluffing to suit the Mien would be more substantive and satisfying than a Specialty. Not necessarily arguing in favor of handing out a free Merit instead or anything, just musing to myself. That said, this does make me wonder. Are there plans or drafts for Changeling-focused Merits in the book that could be useful for reflecting those relatively incidental bits and pieces?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T18:21:54-07:00","id":504910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=504906#post504906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That said, you're right that there do have to be more interesting and substantive ways to reflect that sort of thing. At the least, taking a Merit or two and refluffing to suit the Mien would be more substantive and satisfying than a Specialty. Not necessarily arguing in favor of handing out a free Merit instead or anything, just musing to myself. That said, this does make me wonder. Are there plans or drafts for Changeling-focused Merits in the book that could be useful for reflecting those relatively incidental bits and pieces?</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't read Merits yet. So, I don't know. This is literally the first Second Edition book where I haven't personally written the Merits. So, I'm going to keep a keen eye on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T19:35:58-07:00","id":504947,"title":"","content":"THe idea has been updating and consolidating a lot of stuff from the books,and stuff like that appeared in other books, soooooooooo probably some of that stuff appears.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T00:40:59-07:00","id":505119,"title":"","content":"One thing I enjoyed about the full write ups of kiths in Winter Masques was the small section under each kith offering a list of several mythological creatures that might well fit the overall concept of that kith. While it might be difficult with some of the kiths you are considering here (the Greys and Ifrit, for instance, given their already rather specific placement in pop culture and mythology) I would love to see a similar list included for these kith entries as well","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T07:25:29-07:00","id":505430,"title":"","content":"Probably not possible for the word count of this book. Maybe a future supplement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T07:30:52-07:00","id":505439,"title":"","content":"I actually like the idea of &quot;fads&quot; in the Gentry regarding kiths, it actually helps remind the reader that the True Fae do socialize and acquire preferences, perhaps even to the point of social status demanding something of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T18:00:11-07:00","id":507448,"title":"","content":"What if razor hands got armor piercing for a round instead of doing aggravated damage? It makes for a strong but more situational blessing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T16:56:28-07:00","id":511309,"title":"","content":"Do we know if it will be possible to have several kiths like with the old Dual Kith merit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T17:23:29-07:00","id":511337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=511309#post511309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we know if it will be possible to have several kiths like with the old Dual Kith merit?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the last we heard was that it's still under consideration, but David wants to see how the current schema works as-is with playtesters. Once he knows how the basic foundation functions, he can consider options that modify it, like Dual Kith.<br /> <br /> Even if he decides against it, that introductory section in the Kiths sample seems to encourage creating new Kiths by mixing-and-matching mechanical parts from existing Kiths. That feels like it could do the trick just fine.<br /> <br /> As an aside, neat avatar. Izzat a platypus?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T17:30:01-07:00","id":511343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=511337#post511337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the last we heard was that it's still under consideration, but David wants to see how the current schema works as-is with playtesters. Once he knows how the basic foundation functions, he can consider options that modify it, like Dual Kith.<br /> <br /> Even if he decides against it, that introductory section in the Kiths sample seems to encourage creating new Kiths by mixing-and-matching mechanical parts from existing Kiths. That feels like it could do the trick just fine.<br /> <br /> As an aside, neat avatar. Izzat a platypus?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's an Eliotrope from the Wakfu MMORPG. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T17:43:57-07:00","id":511350,"title":"","content":"Ahh, there we go. XD The full-size image made that much clearer; this forum has a tendency to scrunch things. The avatar remains neat, regardless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T18:23:30-07:00","id":511392,"title":"","content":"Why, thank you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T09:07:55-07:00","id":516229,"title":"","content":"OK, so I'm definitely not caught up on this thread yet. So I could easily have missed something. Very, very easily.<br /> <br /> I'm just a bit concerned about the 'description' of the various seemings if they're X kith. Because I know from past play experiences people tend to take stuff like that pretty literally, unless there's a very clear case of 'this is just a guideline, individuals could look completely different limited only to your imagination' that I missed. Like a Fairest Nightsinger being toned and such, or really, whatever.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, yeah. These are freaking awesome. And I'm in the camp rather hoping there won't be Dual Kith anymore, because these are much more broad, and in the past that tended to be what everyone and their dog would take (Admittedly, a lot of that was stuff like wanting to be a Fairest, but have an Elemental kith appearance and ability as much as it was twinking)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/448-dulahan","name":"Dulahan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T08:45:44-07:00","id":517050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dulahan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=516229#post516229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, so I'm definitely not caught up on this thread yet. So I could easily have missed something. Very, very easily.<br /> <br /> I'm just a bit concerned about the 'description' of the various seemings if they're X kith. Because I know from past play experiences people tend to take stuff like that pretty literally, unless there's a very clear case of 'this is just a guideline, individuals could look completely different limited only to your imagination' that I missed. Like a Fairest Nightsinger being toned and such, or really, whatever.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, yeah. These are freaking awesome. And I'm in the camp rather hoping there won't be Dual Kith anymore, because these are much more broad, and in the past that tended to be what everyone and their dog would take (Admittedly, a lot of that was stuff like wanting to be a Fairest, but have an Elemental kith appearance and ability as much as it was twinking)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Kiths may be somewhat broader, but many archetypes can only be represented by the associations of several kiths, especially since the Seemings now serve a different function.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T09:05:00-07:00","id":517054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=498503#post498503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I considered a Resistance or Finesse Attribute. Not sure though. Not given it much thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's not too late to reply to this. I'd put my vote on a Finesse attribute.<br /> <br /> While Resistance makes sense as coming out of your durance; Finesse will be far more useful during the game.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T18:08:10-07:00","id":517472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=517054#post517054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's not too late to reply to this. I'd put my vote on a Finesse attribute.<br /> <br /> While Resistance makes sense as coming out of your durance; Finesse will be far more useful during the game.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I totally agree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T07:37:23-07:00","id":606554,"title":"","content":"So... I think it's been implied that ALL 1e kiths will be included in the 2e book? Is that actually the case, or was I reading between the lines upside down?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6848-taveena","name":"Taveena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T08:29:38-07:00","id":606643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taveena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=606554#post606554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... I think it's been implied that ALL 1e kiths will be included in the 2e book? Is that actually the case, or was I reading between the lines upside down?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been confirmed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The qualifier is that that some Kiths will be merged for reasons of redundancy. For instance, 1e's Razorhand and Hunterheart are both covered by 2e's Razorhand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T09:17:20-07:00","id":606667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=606643#post606643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's been confirmed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The qualifier is that that some Kiths will be merged for reasons of redundancy. For instance, 1e's Razorhand and Hunterheart are both covered by 2e's Razorhand.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wait, they're calling it Razorhand instead of Hunterheart? ...But wouldn't the latter be better word-wise because it's more general in nature?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T09:42:13-07:00","id":606690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=606667#post606667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, they're calling it Razorhand instead of Hunterheart? ...But wouldn't the latter be better word-wise because it's more general in nature?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would have been my preference, but I can also see it both ways. &quot;Razorhand&quot; directly identifies it as being about causing harm, whereas &quot;Hunterheart&quot; in a vacuum might be expected to offer more bonuses to pursuing and harrying one's chosen quarry. Which does feel like it's a pretty robust area for a Kith now that I think about it.<br /> <br /> Anyway, at least based on the preview draft, Razorhand is where they settled. I recall Dave mentioning the possibility that old Kith names might still be in common use for some Seeming variants. <span style=\"font-size:12px\">It didn't come up in the preview, but I don't think that point is written in stone.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kiths preview</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><b>Razorhand</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>You made me; you gave me my shiny claws and forced me to kill. Now these same claws are going to taste your perfect blood.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Razorhands were created as killers. Some Gentry wanted bodyguards who could swiftly dispatch any threat, others desired assassins able to slay their victims with a single blow but all wished to create exceptionally deadly changelings. Their Keepers made the changeling's body into a living weapon. While some embrace pacifism after their escape, in Acradia, their Keepers forced razorhands to murder dozens of changelings and to also eliminate their enemies among the Gentry. Regardless of their Seeming, all razorhands look deadly and have blades, claws or perhaps shards of crimson glass attached to their hands or fingers.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022 Beast: A sleek and predatory carnivore with short fur, sharp fangs and exceptionally long claws. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022 Darkling: A sharp-faced furtive-looking individual with pointed teeth, exaggerated features, and long fingers. Each hand has a sixth finger normally kept folded against the palm. This finger is a shining blade of pale bone. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022 Ogre: A strong and deadly-looking brute with a large spurs of sharpened bone along the edges of each of her hands</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Blessing: </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Their natural weapon does Wyrd/2 damage. If they spend a point of Glamour, their next attack with this weapon does Aggravated damage and for the next scene it shines and glitters in a manner that gives them +2 to all Intimidation rolls.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Looking it over again, I'd have also preferred less of an emphasis on, &quot;it's always something sharp on their fingers,&quot; in the fluff. Sometimes fangs, horns and other natural weapons are just a better fit for a concept. At least there's nothing in the crunch to prevent someone who'd prefer to go for that.<br /> <br /> Unless the natural weapon was intentionally hand-focused for balance reasons? Not sure I see it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T10:29:31-07:00","id":606801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=606643#post606643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's been confirmed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The qualifier is that that some Kiths will be merged for reasons of redundancy. For instance, 1e's Razorhand and Hunterheart are both covered by 2e's Razorhand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neat. And presumably the 3 different 'can hold breath' kiths will also be merged.<br /> <br /> I presume for a fang-based 1e Hunterheart, they'd instead take the Gristlegrinder or Oni kiths in 2e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6848-taveena","name":"Taveena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T11:13:43-07:00","id":606852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taveena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=606801#post606801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neat. And presumably the 3 different 'can hold breath' kiths will also be merged.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aye, that seems the thrust of the plan. Or, as an alternative, more than one Kith may wind up with the capability, but at least one as more of a side thing to what they're actually about. e.g. An Ifrit and a Fireheart each have something to do with fire, but the former is much more about controlling the power of flame, and for the latter fire-starting is secondary to being quick-witted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I presume for a fang-based 1e Hunterheart, they'd instead take the Gristlegrinder or Oni kiths in 2e? </div> </div> </div>Aye, that's very plausible. I've had little personal interest in Ogres and therefore completely forgot those guys. Though, given the premium on space, I suspect they'll do something different from 2e Razorhand.<br /> <br /> Also something I forgot about<b></b>: there's that bit from early in the preview draft that makes clear the whole thing is very friendly to customization. I could easily see picking some coherent composite of capabilities from multiple Kiths to get the best reflection of a concept, so long as balance is kept in mind. I suspect this will be the recommendation for what were previously dual-Kith characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Per ZealousChristian24's note, tweaked the Ifrit and Fireheart example. 07-29-2015, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T11:46:23-07:00","id":606893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=606852#post606852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. e.g. An Ifrit and a Fireheart can each start a fire, but the former is much more powerful and flexible about it, and for the latter it's secondary to being quick-witted.</div> </div> </div> </div> Forgive the pedantry, but since the Ifrit have only the 3-Dot version of Psychokinesis, they can't create fire, only manipulate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T11:57:24-07:00","id":606896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/495557-open-development-kiths?p=606893#post606893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Forgive the pedantry, but since the Ifrit have only the 3-Dot version of Psychokinesis, they can't create fire, only manipulate it.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a long-time pedant myself, this is forgiven and appreciated! I haven't looked over the GMC updates in any particular detail, so the correction is welcome.<br /> EDIT: Updated original post a smidge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 07-29-2